arrow_pure_helpers_are_imported_from_nodes_inputs`, `test_no_import_from_any_other_nodes_or_routing_or_workbook_module`, `test_no_langchain_provider_sdk_or_direct_http_imports`, `test_no_product_node_or_guard_identifiers_appear_in_source`, `test_build_curriculum_factory_graph_is_the_only_graph_builder_referenced`, `test_graph_builder_is_called_at_most_once_per_execution_path`.\n  - `test_plan26_cli.py:168` `test_no_legacy_simulation_or_session_bridge_or_custom_controller_flags` (checks `--test-static`, `--test-simulated-all`, `--interrupt-after`, etc. absent from `--help`).\n  - `test_plan26_topology.py:830` `test_production_graph_imports_contain_no_fallback_controller`, `:865` `test_only_one_builder_and_one_compile_call_exist`.\n  - `test_plan26_cli.py:395` `test_a_plan25_shaped_root_is_refused_and_left_byte_identical`, `:731` `test_static_import_audit_evidence`, `:745` `test_plan25_root_refusal_evidence`.\n- **Verdict**: reuse-as-is — this row is fully proven by the CLI static-AST-audit machinery (`ast.parse(CLI_SOURCE)`, `_imported_names()`); a wrapper that imports/re-asserts the CLI's own audit is sufficient, or just cite these directly.\n\n### `test_external_data_authorization_precedes_transmission`\n- **Existing coverage**: `test_plan26_transport.py:298` `test_missing_or_mismatched_authorization_makes_zero_calls(tmp_path, mutation)`; `test_plan26_egress.py:82` `test_record_rejects_unknown_provider_and_undeclared_data_class`, `:108` `test_authorization_fails_closed_for_every_scope_mismatch` (7-way parametrized: absent/wrong-run/wrong-digest/wrong-output/provider-not-authorized/data-class-not-authorized/expired), `:323` `test_unauthorized_retrieval_makes_no_connection`.\n- **API**: `egress.authorize_transmission(record, provider=, data_classes=, curriculum_digest=, run_id=, output_root=)`, `egress.AuthorizationRecord`, `egress.EgressGuard`, `egress.SourceRetriever`.\n- **Verdict**: reuse-as-is; \"fail before process/network call\" is the exact framing of `test_unauthorized_retrieval_makes_no_connection` + `test_missing_or_mismatched_authorization_makes_zero_calls`.\n\n### `test_worker_context_is_structurally_bounded`\n- **Existing coverage**: `test_plan26_transport.py:325` `test_sandboxed_worker_cannot_read_repository_output_or_secrets` (uses `tp.prove_workspace_isolation(workspace=, home=, forbidden_paths=[repo_file, sibling_unit_file, parent_history_file, secret_env])` → asserts `proof[\"readable_forbidden_paths\"] == []`, `proof[\"enforced\"] is True`); `:351` `test_capability_proof_is_satisfied_on_this_host` (`tp.prove_transport_capabilities`); `:693` `test_workspace_contains_only_the_authorized_staging_set`; `:729` `test_staged_input_names_cannot_escape_or_shadow`; `:742` `test_undeclared_worker_writes_are_rejected`; `:755` `test_worker_environment_is_allowlisted_over_a_temporary_home`; `:369` `test_the_real_cli_starts_sandboxed_yet_cannot_read_outside_the_workspace` (real `codex`/`gemini`, `@requires_sandbox`-gated).\n- **Verdict**: reuse-as-is — `test_sandboxed_worker_cannot_read_repository_output_or_secrets` is *literally* \"sibling files visible in worker\" already, right down to naming a sibling unit's `accepted.json`.\n\n### `test_dual_persistence_correlation`\n- **Existing coverage**: `test_plan26_persistence.py::TestCorruptionBlocksRecovery` — `test_a_healthy_root_verifies_on_both_layers`, `test_corrupt_sqlite_blocks_recovery_and_is_not_repaired` (checkpoint corrupt, append log fine → `P.CheckpointCorrupt` on `verify_checkpoint_integrity`/`verify_persistence_integrity`/`prepare_episode_invocation(resume=True)`, and proves the corrupted DB is *not silently repaired* via digest-equality), `test_corrupt_append_log_blocks_recovery_and_is_not_repaired` (converse case: checkpoint fine, ledger corrupt), `test_a_truncated_append_log_is_detected`, `test_evidence_log_corruption_alone_blocks_recovery`.\n- **API**: `P.verify_checkpoint_integrity`, `P.verify_persistence_integrity(output_root, evidence_store)`, `P.EpisodeLeaseLedger(output_root).audit()`, `P.AdmissionLedger(output_root).audit()`.\n- **Verdict**: reuse-as-is — this is a near-literal match, both directions of the \"converse\" already exist.\n\n### `test_resume_bootstrap_skips_fresh_write_once_nodes`\n- **Existing coverage** (partial, structural only): `test_plan26_topology.py:229-235` static edges prove `D00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE -> D01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS` (fresh) and `D00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE -> D00R_REVALIDATE_RESUME_IDENTITY -> D03_PROVE_CAPABILITIES` (resume) exist as distinct static branches (`routing.py:117-131` confirms: `\"resume\": \"D00R_REVALIDATE_RESUME_IDENTITY\"` skips `D01`/`D02` entirely, going straight to `D03`). `test_plan26_unit_graph.py:1270-1271` (`test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_langgraph`) asserts `result[\"trace\"].count(\"D01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS\") == 1` and `\"D00R_REVALIDATE_RESUME_IDENTITY\" not in result[\"trace\"]` — but only for a **fresh** episode, not across a fresh→resume pair of the same run. `test_plan26_deterministic_nodes.py:1699` `test_d00r_admits_an_identical_resume_identity`, `:1734/1765/1788` D01 unit tests, `:1887/1920` D04 unit tests — all node-level, not a real two-episode graph run. `test_plan26_persistence.py::TestEpisodeLifecycle.test_each_episode_gets_a_new_thread_with_empty_langgraph_state` proves episode-2 gets a fresh empty thread and `bootstrap_kind == BOOTSTRAP_RESUME`, but doesn't run the *real compiled unit-path graph* through D01 for episode 2 to prove it's never re-entered, nor does it check `created_at` (a write-once global field) is unchanged.\n- **Verdict**: **needs-new-test.** Nothing currently runs `_run_episode` (or equivalent) twice against the same `output_root`/`run_id` — once fresh, once via `resume=True` with `P.prepare_episode_invocation(..., resume=True, read_view=...)` — and asserts (a) `trace.count(\"D01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS\")` stays `1` across the whole *run* (not just episode 1), (b) `state[\"created_at\"]` (or another declared write-once global field) is byte-identical after the resume episode, (c) `D00R` runs on the resume episode. Build this by composing `_build_episode_fixture` + `_run_episode` (episode 1, fresh) then a second `_prepare_episode`-style call with `resume=True` reusing `P.prepare_episode_invocation(output_root=..., lock=..., resume=True, read_view=P.ReadOnlyCheckpointView(compiled, saver))` from `test_plan26_persistence.py::TestEpisodeLifecycle`, then stream episode 2 and check `D01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS not in trace2` and cumulative count across both traces `== 1`. This genuinely needs both harnesses stitched together — the one piece nobody has combined yet.\n\n### `test_orphan_recovery_is_read_only_and_terminal_only`\n- **Existing coverage**: `test_plan26_persistence.py::TestOrphanRecovery` — `test_recovery_after_sigkill_uses_a_new_thread_and_touches_no_product` (real SIGKILL child `ORPHAN_CHILD`, `_tree_snapshot` before/after equality over product bytes), `test_recovery_services_raise_on_any_touch` (`P.build_recovery_services()` returns `renderer`/`source_retriever`/`transport_registry`, every attribute/call raises `P.RecoveryServiceForbidden`), `test_a_recovery_runtime_context_carries_only_forbidden_product_services`, `test_the_read_only_view_cannot_continue_a_prior_thread` (`P.ReadOnlyCheckpointView` has no `invoke`/`stream`/`update_state`/`ainvoke`/`batch`), `test_persistence_module_never_calls_invoke_or_update_state` (AST scan), `test_persistence_module_imports_no_product_or_model_module`. Also `test_plan26_unit_graph.py:1812` `test_a_hard_crash_is_recovered_as_an_orphan_without_continuing_its_thread` — uses `compiled.stream(...)`, breaks mid-stream after `D04_INITIALIZE_OR_RESUME`, then reads via `P.EpisodeLeaseLedger(...).open_lease()`, `P.ReadOnlyCheckpointView`, `P.extract_prior_episode`, asserts `readout.next` contains no `M0*` node ids.\n- **Gap vs spec row**: spec wants \"orphan recovery tries `invoke(None)`, transport, retrieval, render, or a saved product frontier → test fails before side effect; **only D00/D96/D98 execute**.\" The existing tests prove the *services* raise if touched and the *view* has no invoke method, but no test drives the real recovery episode (`invocation.bootstrap_kind == P.BOOTSTRAP_RECOVER_ORPHAN`) through the compiled graph and asserts the executed node trace is `{D00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE, D96_GRACEFUL_INTERRUPT_GATE, D98_WRITE_TERMINAL}` and nothing else (i.e., D91/D92 boundary — recall `routing.py:501` `route_initialize_or_resume`: \"fresh initialization to D05, validated resume import to D92\" — orphan recovery specifically must never reach D92 or beyond either).\n- **Verdict**: **needs-new-test** — compose `TestOrphanRecovery`'s real-SIGKILL child pattern with `_run_episode`-style streaming of the *actual* production graph in recovery mode, and assert trace ⊆ `{\"D00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE\", \"D96_GRACEFUL_INTERRUPT_GATE\", \"D98_WRITE_TERMINAL\"}`. Existing `test_a_hard_crash_is_recovered_as_an_orphan_without_continuing_its_thread` gets most of the way there but stops at *reading* the orphan, not *re-invoking* the compiled graph in recovery mode to completion.\n\n### `test_checkpoint_thread_and_namespace_contract`\n- **Existing coverage**: `test_plan26_persistence.py::TestCheckpointConfiguration` — `test_thread_ids_follow_the_frozen_format` (`P.episode_thread_id(\"run-x\", 1) == \"run-x:episode:000001\"`, `P.recovery_thread_id(\"run-x\", 7) == \"run-x:recover:7\"`, rejects ordinal `0`/`-1` via `P.PersistenceError`), `test_invoke_config_is_exactly_thread_id_and_root_namespace` (`P.invoke_config(...) == {\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": ..., \"checkpoint_ns\": \"\"}}`, `P.CHECKPOINT_NS == \"\"`), `test_a_real_checkpoint_is_stored_under_the_root_namespace` (real SQL query `SELECT DISTINCT thread_id, checkpoint_ns FROM checkpoints`).\n- **Gap**: spec wants \"checkpoint namespace differs from root `\\\"\\\"`, or thread ID lacks run/episode relation → invocation rejected.\" No test currently constructs a *malformed* thread id (e.g. one with no `run_id` prefix, or a non-`\":episode:NNNNNN\"`/`\":recover:N\"` suffix) and asserts something explicitly *rejects invocation* (as opposed to merely computing the correct format). `P.episode_thread_id`/`recovery_thread_id` are pure formatters, not validators of externally-supplied thread ids.\n- **Verdict**: **needs-new-test** — check whether `runtime/langgraph_factory/persistence.py` has a validator for an *incoming* thread id/namespace (grep didn't surface one distinct from the formatters); if none exists, this row may need to assert the invariant is enforced structurally (only `episode_thread_id`/`recovery_thread_id`/`invoke_config` are ever used to build a `config`, i.e., an AST/call-site audit similar to `test_persistence_module_never_calls_invoke_or_update_state`), since there may be no runtime-checked \"reject a bad namespace\" path — flag this as a possible spec-vs-implementation gap to verify before writing the test.\n\n### `test_visual_send_reduce_barrier`\n- **Existing coverage**: \n  - \"mixed static/dynamic predecessor join is structurally legitimate\": `test_plan26_unit_graph.py:797` `test_the_two_map_reduce_return_edges_are_normal_edges` — explicitly asserts both `(\"D11_CREATE_DETERMINISTIC_VISUALS\", \"D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN\")` and `(\"M04_CREATE_UNIT_VISUALS\", \"D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN\")` are *normal* (non-conditional) edges into the same barrier.\n  - \"empty visual subset\": `test_plan26_unit_graph.py:1010` and `test_plan26_topology.py:752`, both named `test_an_empty_deterministic_visual_subset_routes_straight_to_the_barrier`.\n  - \"guard-level rejection of malformed/mixed dispatch\": `test_plan26_topology.py:701` `test_a_fanout_guard_refuses_an_unstaged_or_mixed_dispatch`.\n  - Indirect \"executes once\" evidence: `test_plan26_unit_graph.py:1408` `test_a_visual_denominator_permutation_produces_an_identical_admitted_head` — real two-episode run, asserts `trace.count(\"D11_CREATE_DETERMINISTIC_VISUALS\") == 1` and `trace.count(\"M04_CREATE_UNIT_VISUALS\") == 1` and a single `join[0][\"result\"] == \"PASS\"` record with `denominator_size == actual_size == 2`, but **does not** assert `trace.count(\"D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN\") == 1` directly.\n- **Gap**: no test literally asserts `D12` fires exactly once in a real superstep despite receiving both a static (D11) and dynamic (M04 `Send`-fanout) contribution in the same map/reduce round.\n- **Verdict**: **needs-new-test** (or a thin wrapper) — add `trace.count(\"D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN\") == 1` to a real `_run_episode`-style run with the existing two-visual `DECLARED_VISUALS` fixture (one deterministic member via D11, one model member via M04), citing `test_the_two_map_reduce_return_edges_are_normal_edges` for the \"mixed join is topologically valid\" half and `test_an_empty_deterministic_visual_subset_routes_straight_to_the_barrier` for the empty-subset half.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Key API/fixture cheat-sheet for writing the new file\n\n```python\n# graph / topology\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import graph as G          # G.build_curriculum_factory_graph(engine_root=, output_root=)\n                                                            # G.compiled_topology(compiled) -> {\"edges\": [(src,tgt,conditional), ...]}\n                                                            # G.binding_inventory(), G.build_model_node_context (monkeypatch target)\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import routing as R         # R.decide, R.route_*, R.FANOUT_GUARDS, R.RoutingViolation\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import unit_graph as U       # U.DEFERRED_EDGES, U.UNIT_BRANCHES, U.UNIT_NORMAL_EDGES, U.BLOCKING_GAPS\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import model_nodes as mn     # mn.MODEL_NODE_ADAPTERS, mn.tp (transport module),\n                                                            # mn.build_test_model_node_context(sandbox_root=, responses={})\n                                                            # mn.build_model_node_context (production, refuses fakes)\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes import (NODE_CATALOGUE, domain, inputs, render, review, sources, visuals)\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes import terminal as D98   # D98.write_terminal, D98.validate_terminal_candidate, D98._INTERRUPT_CLASSIFICATIONS\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory.reducers import WriteOnceConflict, write_once\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory.state import FACTORY_STATE_FIELDS, FIELD_REDUCER_CLASSES, FactoryState, RuntimeContext\n\n# persistence (SIGKILL/lock-race/resume harness)\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import persistence as P\n# P.ExecutionLock, P.ExecutionLockUnavailable, P.LOCK_LOSER_EXIT_CODE\n# P.open_checkpoint_saver(output_root), P.checkpoint_db_path, P.execution_lock_path\n# P.episode_thread_id(run_id, ordinal), P.recovery_thread_id(run_id, ordinal), P.invoke_config(thread_id), P.CHECKPOINT_NS\n# P.prepare_episode_invocation(output_root=, lock=, identity_seed=None, resume=False, resume_baseline=None, recomputed=None, read_view=None)\n# P.EpisodeInvocation(.config, .thread_id, .run_id, .episode_ordinal, .bootstrap_kind, .prior_thread_id, .resume_from)\n# P.BOOTSTRAP_FRESH / P.BOOTSTRAP_RESUME / P.BOOTSTRAP_RECOVER_ORPHAN\n# P.ReadOnlyCheckpointView(compiled, saver), P.extract_prior_episode(view, thread_id) -> PriorEpisodeReadout\n# P.EpisodeLeaseLedger(output_root).open_lease()/.open_episode()/.close_episode()/.records()/.audit()\n# P.AdmissionLedger(output_root).admit(key, payload)/.records()/.audit()\n# P.InterruptToken(output_root).install()/.is_set()/.reason/.marker_path/.guard_transmission(...)\n# P.validate_resume_inputs(expected=, observed=) -> raises P.ResumeRefused(.drift_class, .field)\n# P.compute_resume_frontier(readout=, denominators=None, reason=...), P.classify_join_members(expected_keys=, completed_keys=)\n# P.build_interrupt_terminal_candidate(run_id=, episode_id=, frontier=, classification=, heads=, high_water_marks=)\n# P.verify_checkpoint_integrity(output_root), P.verify_persistence_integrity(output_root, evidence_store=None) -> raises P.CheckpointCorrupt\n# P.build_recovery_services() -> {\"renderer\",\"source_retriever\",\"transport_registry\"} all raising P.RecoveryServiceForbidden\n# P.flush_checkpoint_durability(conn, output_root), P.state_digest(values), P.compute_fresh_run_id(identity_seed)\n\n# transport / egress\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import transport as tp\n# tp.FakeCliTransport(sandbox_root=, responses={}, registry=None), tp.load_job_registry()\n# tp.prove_workspace_isolation(workspace=, home=, forbidden_paths=[...]) -> {\"mechanism\",\"readable_forbidden_paths\",\"enforced\"}\n# tp.prove_transport_capabilities(guard=, probe_root=, forbidden_paths=[...], identity_help={...})\n# tp.REPO_ROOT\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import egress as E\n# E.EgressGuard(receipts).install()/.uninstall(), E.ReceiptLog(), E.AuthorizationRecord(...)\n# E.authorize_transmission(record, provider=, data_classes=, curriculum_digest=, run_id=, output_root=)\n# E.MODEL_API_HOSTS, E.AuthorizationDenied, E.EgressDenied, E.SourceRetriever\n\n# repair / acceptance / workbook\nfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import repair, acceptance, workbook\n# repair.MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN, repair.MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS\n# repair.D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS / D18_PLAN_TARGETED_UNIT_REPAIR / D19_ROUTE_UNIT_REPAIR / D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR / D21_RETEST_REQUIRED_DESCENDANTS\n# repair.within_boundary(pointer, allowed), repair.json_pointer_diff(parent, child), repair.finding_fingerprint(owner, boundary, message)\n# acceptance.prove_exact_manifest_coverage(ordered_unit_ids, accepted_unit_receipts, declared_coverage) -> (passed, rejections)\n# acceptance.D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE / D22_ACCEPT_UNIT / D23_CHECKPOINT_ACCEPTED_UNIT\n# workbook.D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE ... D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE, workbook.compute_workbook_denominator\n\n# CLI (import-audit convention)\nimport runtime.run_curriculum as RCLI      # RCLI.main(argv), RCLI.build_parser()\nCLI_AST = ast.parse(Path(inspect.getsourcefile(RCLI)).read_text())  # same pattern as test_plan26_cli.py's ImportGraphAuditTests\n```\n\n### Local harness to (re)build in the new file (nothing importable cross-file today)\nMirror `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`'s private helpers locally (same names is fine, it's a private convention, not an API): `_build_episode_fixture`, `_prepare_episode`, `_run_episode`, `_HarnessContext`, `_ScriptedFakeTransport`/`_scripted_candidate`, `_SwitchableToken`. For the two rows that need a **two-episode** run (`test_resume_bootstrap_skips_fresh_write_once_nodes`, `test_orphan_recovery_is_read_only_and_terminal_only`), you'll need to extend `_run_episode` to accept an existing `output_root`/lock and a `resume=True`/orphan-recovery mode rather than always calling `_prepare_episode` fresh — none of the existing files do this composition, confirming both are genuinely new.\n\nFor the two SIGKILL-based rows reusable from `test_plan26_persistence.py`, copy `_run_child`, `ORPHAN_CHILD` (as a starting template — extend it to run the *real* `build_curriculum_factory_graph` rather than the toy 2-node `StateGraph` it currently uses, if you want the recovery trace to be `{D00,D96,D98}` specifically).","usage":{"total_tokens":143712,"tool_uses":66,"duration_ms":411484},"uuid":"04fb31dd-b2fe-424e-81f2-8e8a96cc253a","session_id":"913d8145-a69b-41ae-866d-8d539cb6c5e2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TfYwPSgaq8ZH6nJTFDz7zX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: tests/runtime/test_plan26_adversarial.py (24 rows, spec 17.2)\n\n## 0. Structural findings (apply to all 24 rows)\n\n**No `conftest.py` anywhere in `tests/` or `tests/runtime/`** (confirmed via `find`). Every `test_plan26_*.py` file is self-contained: each defines its own private (`_`-prefixed) fixtures, fake-transport class, `_Context`/`_HarnessContext` double, and manifest/state builders — duplicated per file rather than shared. `tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py`'s docstring explicitly says it follows \"the convention `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` already established\" for a `test_blocked_*` gap pattern — meaning: copy the *pattern*, don't import the *module*. No test file currently imports another `test_plan26_*` module. `tests/runtime/__init__.py` exists (so cross-file import is technically possible, e.g. `from tests.runtime import test_plan26_unit_graph as UG`), but it would break the established convention — flag this as a decision point rather than assuming it's safe.\n\nAll hash-locked-environment test files open with the same skip guard:\n```python\ntry:\n    import langgraph\n    import langgraph.checkpoint.sqlite\nexcept ModuleNotFoundError as exc:\n    raise unittest.SkipTest(\"plan26 hash-locked environment not installed ...\") from exc\n```\n`test_plan26_adversarial.py` must include this same guard if it touches `langgraph`/`persistence`/`unit_graph`/`graph`.\n\n**The one full end-to-end harness** (real compiled graph, real `StateGraph`, scripted-but-schema-valid model transport) lives in `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py`, all private:\n- `_build_episode_fixture(tmp_path, units=1) -> dict` — builds engine_root/curriculum/manifest/output_root/sandbox on disk, copies real engine contracts (`ENGINE_CONTRACTS`).\n- `_prepare_episode(fixture, *, mode=\"one\", requested=\"U001\") -> (lock, invocation, envelope)` — real `P.ExecutionLock`, real `P.prepare_episode_invocation`, computes `frozen_digest` via `inputs.D01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS`.\n- `_run_episode(monkeypatch, fixture, *, interrupt_after=None) -> dict` with keys `trace`, `updates`, `deferred_frontier`, `state`, `context`, `invocation`, `compiled` — monkeypatches `G.build_model_node_context` to return `_scripted_model_context(sandbox)`, then really calls `G.build_curriculum_factory_graph(...)`, and streams it (`compiled.stream(..., stream_mode=\"updates\", context=context)`), tripping `context.signal_token.trip()` after a named node if `interrupt_after` is given.\n- `_HarnessContext(engine_root, output_root, sandbox)` — `RuntimeContext`-shaped double with real `ArtifactStore`/`EvidenceStore`, `_StubRegistry` (renderer/rasterizer/capability double), `_StubRetriever`, `_SwitchableToken` (`.trip()`/`.is_set()`).\n- `_ScriptedFakeTransport(mn.tp.FakeCliTransport)` + `_scripted_candidate(job_id, projection)` — produces schema-valid canned candidates per job id, still routed through real schema validation (it *is* a `FakeCliTransport`).\n- `REACHABLE_BOUNDARIES`, `UNOBSERVABLE_BOUNDARY`, `MODEL_NODE_IDS = frozenset(mn.MODEL_NODE_ADAPTERS)`.\n\nA **second, sanctioned (non-private) fake-context builder** exists directly in production code: `mn.build_test_model_node_context(sandbox_root=..., responses={...})` in `runtime/langgraph_factory/model_nodes.py`, used e.g. at `tests/runtime/test_plan26_model_nodes.py:1113`. It's simpler (one canned response per job) and is guarded by `_assert_production_transport` so it can never leak into `build_model_node_context` (proven by `test_the_production_context_refuses_a_fake_transport`, `test_only_the_named_test_builder_and_its_guard_mention_the_fake_transport`, `model_nodes.py:1085`).\n\n**SIGINT/crash injection** happens in two different, non-overlapping ways:\n1. In-process, cooperative: `_SwitchableToken`/`P.InterruptToken` — `context.signal_token.trip()` after a node returns; the *next* node boundary observes it via `routing.interrupt_requested`. Used throughout `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` (`_run_episode(..., interrupt_after=...)`) and `test_plan26_persistence.py::TestGracefulInterrupt` (`P.InterruptToken(...).install()`, then literally `signal.raise_signal(signal.SIGINT)` / `SIGTERM`).\n2. Real OS-level SIGKILL via a **child subprocess**: `tests/runtime/test_plan26_persistence.py` has `_run_child(script, *args)` which writes `script` (a `textwrap.dedent`-ed Python source, e.g. `CRASH_CHILD`, `LOCK_CHILD`, `ORPHAN_CHILD`) to a temp file and runs it with `subprocess.run([sys.executable, child_path, str(REPO_ROOT), *args], ...)`; the child kills itself with `os.kill(os.getpid(), signal.SIGKILL)` at a chosen boundary string (`\"before_admit\"`/`\"after_admit\"`/`\"after_checkpoint\"`). This is the *only* place a hard-crash matrix is proven for real.\n\n**Egress-zero / socket proof**: `tests/runtime/test_plan26_egress.py` is real — `EgressGuard(receipts).install()`/`.uninstall()` monkeypatches `socket.socket.connect`/`connect_ex` at the class level (module `runtime/langgraph_factory/egress.py`), and tests literally attempt `socket.create_connection`, `urllib.request.urlopen`, `http.client.HTTPConnection.connect`, and raw `socket.socket().connect_ex(...)` and assert `EgressDenied`/receipted denial (`test_raw_socket_connect_is_denied_and_receipted`, `test_urllib_and_http_client_cannot_route_around_the_broker`, `test_connect_ex_is_also_brokered`, `test_direct_model_endpoint_is_denied` parametrized over `MODEL_API_HOSTS`). It does **not** test HTTP redirects or a literal \"sandbox-bypass\" scenario beyond the OS-level `sandbox-exec` proof living in `test_plan26_transport.py` (`tp.prove_workspace_isolation`, `tp.prove_transport_capabilities`) — DNS rebinding is covered (`test_dns_rebinding_to_an_unpinned_address_is_denied`), oversized-response and non-global-IP resolution are covered.\n\n**Lock-drift / CI proof**: `tests/runtime/test_plan26_lock_drift.py` asserts pin/lock/hash integrity (`test_direct_pins_file_declares_exact_versions`, `test_every_locked_distribution_carries_at_least_one_sha256_hash`, `test_lock_is_installable_with_require_hashes_semantics`, `test_forbidden_distributions_absent_from_lock`) and a **GitHub Actions workflow static-YAML check** (`test_workflow_fails_the_build_on_drift`, `test_workflow_installs_with_require_hashes`, `test_workflow_runs_both_plan26_dependency_tests`). It does not execute the graph; it's a pure supply-chain/CI-config gate. Not directly reusable for any of the 24 rows except as a citation for \"hash-locked environment\" boilerplate.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Per-test mapping\n\n### `test_no_nonproduct_success`\n- **Existing coverage**: `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py:1173` `test_no_node_in_this_path_can_emit_a_product_success_terminal`; `:1198` `test_the_model_path_uses_only_a_test_transport_and_no_product_output_root`; `tests/runtime/test_plan26_transport.py:786` `test_fake_transport_refuses_a_product_root`, `:793` `test_fake_transport_cannot_emit_a_terminal`; `tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py:311` `test_preflight_cannot_emit_product_success`; `tests/runtime/test_plan26_model_nodes.py:1122` `test_the_fake_transport_still_refuses_a_product_root`.\n- **Fixtures**: `_run_episode`/`_build_episode_fixture` (unit_graph.py); `tp.FakeCliTransport(sandbox_root=...)` refuses any root not under system temp (transport.py); `mn.build_test_model_node_context` (model_nodes.py).\n- **Verdict**: reuse-as-is as citations; **needs a thin wrapper test** in the new file that composes these into one adversarial narrative (graph+test-transport+prompt+capability+simulation \"presented as product\" all in one assertion chain) since spec literally names this row as its own case across 4+ files.\n\n### `test_manifest_neutral_dynamic_run`\n- **Existing coverage**: `test_plan26_unit_graph.py:1135` `test_one_mode_computes_the_complete_prerequisite_closure_in_manifest_order` (parametrized over sizes incl. shuffled), `:1160` `test_a_diamond_closure_admits_each_ancestor_exactly_once`; `test_plan26_topology.py:722` `test_no_curriculum_specific_manifest_length_or_order_is_hardcoded`, `:746` `test_the_builder_registers_a_fixed_node_set_independent_of_any_manifest`, `:763` `test_an_exhausted_manifest_routes_to_coverage_proof_at_any_length`.\n- **Fixtures**: `_synthetic_manifest(tmp_path, unit_count, edges=None, shuffle_seed=None)` (unit_graph.py:130) — exactly the \"1/7/41 shuffled/DAG\" generator the spec row wants; parametrize `unit_count` in {1,7,41} and `shuffle_seed` for the new test.\n- **Verdict**: reuse `_synthetic_manifest`-style generator directly (define locally in new file, matching its shape) → **needs-new-test** that specifically drives `unit_count ∈ {1,7,41}` with `shuffle_seed` set, computing closure via `inputs.D02_COMPILE_EFFECTIVE_RUN`.\n\n### `test_models_have_no_control_fields`\n- **Existing coverage**: `test_plan26_model_nodes.py:436` `test_every_projection_is_control_field_free`, `:418` `test_a_poisoned_full_state_cannot_widen_any_projection`, `:517` `test_every_job_schema_is_closed_and_control_free`, `:532` `test_the_adapter_rejects_an_injected_control_field`, `:539` `test_the_adapter_closes_the_one_object_the_schema_leaves_open`; `test_plan26_topology.py:468` `test_a_model_node_holds_no_acceptance_reduction_or_terminal_channel_authority`, `:505` `test_routing_never_lets_a_model_result_name_its_own_destination`, `:550` `test_a_stored_frontier_may_not_name_a_model_node`.\n- **Fixtures**: `tp.FakeCliTransport` schema validation path; job schemas under `runtime/langgraph_factory/schemas`.\n- **Verdict**: reuse-as-is / needs-wrapper — coverage is essentially total; a wrapper test asserting \"a source/model output that proposes next-node/acceptance/terminal is ignored/rejected\" end-to-end via `_run_episode` with a poisoned `_scripted_candidate` would close the \"ignored/rejected schema\" language literally.\n\n### `test_prompts_are_package_relative`\n- **Existing coverage**: `test_plan26_transport.py:264` `test_prompts_resolve_relative_to_the_package_not_the_cwd`, `:280` `test_prompt_path_substitution_is_rejected`, `:286` `test_every_route_has_a_package_prompt_and_schema`.\n- **Fixtures**: `monkeypatch` on cwd; `tp` module constants for prompt roots.\n- **Verdict**: reuse-as-is (near-total). New test can just call these same assertions again or import the pattern — spec explicitly wants \"prompt resolved from cwd or root `prompts/` → preflight/system failure\", which is exactly `test_prompt_path_substitution_is_rejected`.\n\n### `test_malformed_cli_output_fails_closed`\n- **Existing coverage**: `test_plan26_transport.py:526` `test_only_one_clean_json_document_is_accepted(document, failure_class)`, `:554` `test_malformed_result_gets_exactly_one_retry_then_fails`, `:564` `test_schema_invalid_result_gets_exactly_one_retry`, `:575` `test_the_single_retry_can_succeed`, `:589` `test_identity_mismatch_is_never_retried`, `:599` `test_attempt_ledger_refuses_a_third_attempt`; `test_plan26_model_nodes.py:789` `test_a_malformed_result_yields_a_classifiable_failure_not_a_candidate`, `:800` `test_a_retry_traverses_d91_then_d90_before_the_second_transport_call`.\n- **Verdict**: reuse-as-is — \"one bounded retry then failure\" is already pinned exactly by `test_malformed_result_gets_exactly_one_retry_then_fails` + `test_attempt_ledger_refuses_a_third_attempt`.\n\n### `test_executed_model_must_match_route`\n- **Existing coverage**: `test_plan26_transport.py:465` `test_execute_fails_when_the_observed_model_differs_from_the_decision`, `:475` `test_execute_fails_when_identity_cannot_be_observed`, `:423` `test_codex_identity_is_read_from_the_event_stream`, `:430` `test_codex_reroute_supersedes_the_initial_session_model`, `:437` `test_codex_stream_without_a_model_is_unobservable`, `:443/:450` gemini equivalents.\n- **Verdict**: reuse-as-is; near-complete.\n\n### `test_same_family_review_rejec