cted, test_repair_boundary_and_immutability, test_local_repair_is_targeted, test_repair_bound_reserved_first, test_resume_preserves_accepted_bytes, test_duplicate_continuation_prevented, test_workbook_exact_manifest_coverage, test_workbook_repair_cannot_change_unit, test_no_second_production_factory, test_external_data_authorization_precedes_transmission, test_worker_context_is_structurally_bounded, test_dual_persistence_correlation, test_resume_bootstrap_skips_fresh_write_once_nodes, test_orphan_recovery_is_read_only_and_terminal_only, test_checkpoint_thread_and_namespace_contract, test_visual_send_reduce_barrier\n\nNone of these exact function names exist anywhere yet (confirmed via grep). But related/adjacent behavior may already be tested under different names in the existing files: tests/runtime/test_plan26_state_reducers.py, test_plan26_topology.py, test_plan26_transport.py, test_plan26_egress.py, test_plan26_persistence.py, test_plan26_deterministic_nodes.py, test_plan26_model_nodes.py, test_plan26_unit_graph.py, test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py, test_plan26_workbook.py, test_plan26_cli.py, test_plan26_api_contract.py, test_plan26_lock_drift.py.\n\nI need you to research and report back (do NOT write any code, this is read-only research):\n\n1. For each of the 24 test names above, identify: (a) which existing test file(s) already cover the same behavior (even if under a different function name) — quote the exact existing test function name(s) and file:line; (b) what fixtures/helpers those existing tests use (e.g. a fake-transport builder, a temp output_root fixture, a manifest builder, a way to construct/compile the graph, a way to invoke episodes/supersteps, a SIGINT/crash injection helper) — give exact names and where they're defined (conftest.py or in-file); (c) whether the existing coverage is complete enough to satisfy the row, or whether a genuinely new test is needed in test_plan26_adversarial.py.\n\n2. Specifically look for: how tests build a compiled