{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vmu3BZwmGkEaRV1smZXAE8","type":"tool_result","content":"750\t  --output-root outputs/plan26-full \\\n751\t  --resume \\\n752\t  --authorization external-data.authorization.json\n753\t```\n754\t\n755\tThe Arduino manifest is an acceptance example only. Graph modules may contain none of `arduino`, `L12`, `L01`, `35`, or an assumed sequence. The resolver also accepts a curriculum directory and selects its exact active manifest by the existing repository contract; the identity stores the resolved manifest path/hash.\n756\t\n757\tA fresh live output root must not exist or must be an existing empty directory containing no run identity. Preflight treats its output path as a collision probe and does not populate it. Resume requires an existing Plan 26 identity, checkpoint DB, episode ledger, and a resumable last terminal. `--unit`, `--all`, and `--resume` are mutually exclusive; resume derives original mode/target and refuses overrides.\n758\t\n759\tEvery invocation prints exactly one JSON object to stdout. A live result contains `contract_version`, `run_id`, `episode_id`, `terminal`, `mode`, `requested_unit_id`, `accepted_receipt` or `release_receipt`, `checkpoint_id`, `evidence_index_hash`, and `output_root`; human diagnostics go to stderr. Exit codes are section 14. When Codex/Gemini/retrieval credentials, executable identity, observable model identity, or external-data authorization are unavailable, preflight reports specific failed capability and exits 3. A live run that somehow reaches D03 with the same absence writes `SYSTEM_FAILURE` before transmission; it never simulates or switches family.\n760\t\n761\t## 17. Test and adversarial acceptance matrix\n762\t\n763\t### 17.1 Test layers\n764\t\n765\t| Layer | Required proof |\n766\t|---|---|\n767\t| reducer/unit | write-once conflict, disjoint union associativity, head parent/version enforcement, monotonic counters/status, terminal once, exact partition |\n768\t| graph topology | START/END ownership, all node IDs/edges, exactly eight model job types, models cannot reach guarded authorities, arbitrary manifest lengths/DAGs |\n769\t| fake-transport integration | complete branch/loop/fan-out behavior, failure classification, targeted invalidation, bounds, structured receipts; terminal is marked `test_evidence_only` and cannot be copied to product output |\n770\t| live transport contract | isolated staging, package prompt resolution, CLI arguments, observed model identity, JSON/schema failure, timeouts, provider authorization |\n771\t| interruption/resume | each superstep and each fan-out member, pending-write reuse, crash recovery, identity drift refusal, lock/duplicate prevention, accepted-byte preservation |\n772\t| rendering/product | real renderer/rasterizer, positive contiguous pages, every-page inspections and cross-family reviews, actual PDF hashes, exact workbook coverage/final audit |\n773\t| live product acceptance | authorized real Codex/Gemini/source/render execution on actual curriculum; only this layer can establish curriculum quality |\n774\t\n775\tFake models prove orchestration only. They cannot establish source truth, curriculum quality, review independence in substance, `UNIT_ACCEPTED`, or `COMPLETE` in a release output root. Test graph outputs use a separate temporary root and an unmistakable non-product terminal envelope.\n776\t\n777\t### 17.2 Mandatory adversarial cases\n778\t\n779\t| Attack/fault | Expected result | Verification test |\n780\t|---|---|---|\n781\t| graph/test/prompt/capability/simulation presented as product | no success terminal | `test_no_nonproduct_success` |\n782\t| manifest has 1, 7, or 41 shuffled/DAG units | exact computed order/closure | `test_manifest_neutral_dynamic_run` |\n783\t| source/model output proposes next node/acceptance/terminal | ignored/rejected schema | `test_models_have_no_control_fields` |\n784\t| prompt resolved from cwd or root `prompts/` | preflight/system failure | `test_prompts_are_package_relative` |\n785\t| malformed/multiple/trailing CLI JSON | one bounded retry then failure | `test_malformed_cli_output_fails_closed` |\n786\t| decided model differs from observed executed model | system failure | `test_executed_model_must_match_route` |\n787\t| reviewer family equals any author/repair family | system failure | `test_same_family_review_rejected` |\n788\t| missing/duplicate/extra/stale/cross-unit source or visual member | join failure; no admission | `test_exact_fanout_denominators` |\n789\t| page 0, gap, duplicate, wrong hash, or omitted review page | no acceptance | `test_every_unit_page_required`, `test_every_workbook_page_required` |\n790\t| stale artifact/check/review/receipt hash | no acceptance/system integrity failure | `test_stale_hash_rejected` |\n791\t| repair changes unrelated pointer/file or parent in place | system failure; parent unchanged | `test_repair_boundary_and_immutability` |\n792\t| local defect attempts whole-unit regeneration | request/admission rejected | `test_local_repair_is_targeted` |\n793\t| counter/fingerprint exceeds frozen bound | convergence exhausted before activation | `test_repair_bound_reserved_first` |\n794\t| resume tries to rewrite accepted unit/PDF | system failure; bytes unchanged | `test_resume_preserves_accepted_bytes` |\n795\t| two resume processes | one lock winner; loser exits 2 | `test_duplicate_continuation_prevented` |\n796\t| workbook missing/extra/reordered accepted unit | no assembly/complete | `test_workbook_exact_manifest_coverage` |\n797\t| workbook repair changes any unit hash | system failure | `test_workbook_repair_cannot_change_unit` |\n798\t| legacy FSM/session bridge/simulation flag on Plan 26 | invocation rejected | `test_no_second_production_factory` |\n799\t| absent OpenAI/Google/retrieval authorization | fail before process/network call | `test_external_data_authorization_precedes_transmission` |\n800\t| sibling files visible in worker | preflight/system isolation failure | `test_worker_context_is_structurally_bounded` |\n801\t| checkpoint valid but append log corrupt, or converse | no acceptance/resume | `test_dual_persistence_correlation` |\n802\t| resume input reaches D01 or changes `created_at`/another global write-once field | topology/reducer failure; D01 activation count remains one for the run | `test_resume_bootstrap_skips_fresh_write_once_nodes` |\n803\t| orphan recovery tries `invoke(None)`, transport, retrieval, render, or a saved product frontier | test fails before side effect; only D00/D96/D98 execute | `test_orphan_recovery_is_read_only_and_terminal_only` |\n804\t| checkpoint namespace differs from root `\"\"`, or thread ID lacks run/episode relation | invocation rejected | `test_checkpoint_thread_and_namespace_contract` |\n805\t| mixed static/dynamic visual predecessor join or empty visual subset | topology test rejects mixed join; barrier executes exactly once per map superstep and handles empty subset | `test_visual_send_reduce_barrier` |\n806\t\n807\tIntegration must inject SIGINT before/after each node and during each CLI process. It verifies one terminal per episode, `StateSnapshot.next/tasks` reconstruction, no repeated valid fan-out work, current counters, and identical accepted hashes after resume. Hard-crash tests seed snapshots whose saved next task is each of M01–M08 and prove recovery makes zero external calls before D03 in the later episode. API-contract tests pin the `StateGraph`, sequential `Send`-worker-to-reducer pattern, `SqliteSaver.get_tuple` pending writes, episode-derived threads, root namespace, `get_state`, and history behavior used here.\n808\t\n809\t## 18. Migration and retirement boundary\n810\t\n811\tPlan 26 activation is an atomic production cutover, not a long-lived dual run:\n812\t\n813\t| Module/mechanism | Status after activation |\n814\t|---|---|\n815\t| `runtime/io.py`, deterministic portions of `checks.py`, curriculum verifiers/schemas/contracts | reused unchanged unless an interface adapter is required |\n816\t| `controller.CurriculumRuntime`, `routing.Selector`, `lesson_render.py`, `pdf_inspect.py`, `visual_maps.py`, logger, safe workbook concatenation primitive | adapted behind Plan 26 nodes/services |\n817\t| `model_worker.py` | replaced in production by `langgraph_factory.transport`; retained temporarily for Plan 25 historical tests |\n818\t| `curriculum_factory_graph.py` custom controller | replaced in production; retained read-only for Plan 25 historical/test compatibility |\n819\t| `factory_state.py`, `checkpoint.py`, `run_state.py` orchestration/lifecycle roles | replaced by typed graph state/SqliteSaver; historical tests may retain imports |\n820\t| `session_bridge.py`, `CROSS_FAMILY_BYPASS`, `ACCEPTED_PENDING_REVIEW` | prohibited from production Plan 26 |\n821\t| `controller.simulate`, CLI `--test-simulated*`, capability-only finalization | moved to test-only entry points or rejected by production CLI |\n822\t| legacy `workbook.assemble()` completion/terminal behavior | prohibited; only a nonterminal concatenate primitive may be extracted |\n823\t\n824\tCutover gates: the full Plan 26 tests pass; a live authorized acceptance run produces actual accepted artifacts; import/dependency audit shows `runtime.run_curriculum` reaches only `build_curriculum_factory_graph`; CLI help exposes no legacy simulation path; and a static call-graph test proves no second production factory. Only then may Plan 26 become active. Existing Plan 25 output roots remain readable historical evidence but are not resumable by Plan 26 because their identity/checkpoint format differs. No automatic migration fabricates LangGraph checkpoints.\n825\t\n826\t## 19. Traceability matrix\n827\t\n828\t| Prompt requirement | Specification | Node/state | Proposed implementation | Verification |\n829\t|---|---|---|---|---|"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NeCmjuxKDcAbksKJ6Yq96c","session_id":"913d8145-a69b-41ae-866d-8d539cb6c5e2","uuid":"9c50ae31-a1a0-40b6-96ad-6dc0c2529114","timestamp":"2026-08-12T15:12:39.578Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write test_plan26_adversarial.py"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CzjBSJn16zsfr6H5CFqTBR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Plan 26 per-unit path gate (spec sections 8.1, 8.2, 10, 11.3-11.4): N30's wiring.\n2\t\n3\tEvery topology assertion runs against the one real `CompiledStateGraph` that\n4\t`graph.build_curriculum_factory_graph` produces from the real N22/N23 callables,\n5\tand every denominator assertion runs the real node body and the real guard. A\n6\tmock would prove that a stand-in joins correctly, which is the one thing this\n7\tfile exists to rule out.\n8\t\n9\tThe episode now really executes: `_run_episode` streams the one compiled\n10\tproduction graph from D00 to a written terminal, against `RuntimeContext` test\n11\tdoubles and a test-only model transport. Three kinds of test live here:\n12\t\n13\t- assertions about the unit topology that is genuinely registered now,\n14\t- assertions that run one real episode of the real compiled graph, and\n15\t- explicitly named `test_blocked_*` guards that assert the *current, broken*\n16\t  behaviour of a dependency outside this node's write set.\n17\t\n18\tEach blocked guard names its owner and the exact rework that inverts it, and\n19\t`test_every_blocking_gap_is_declared_with_an_owner_and_rework_edge` keeps that\n20\tlist total, so a gap cannot be quietly forgotten once it is fixed: the guard\n21\tfails the moment the rework lands, which is what forces this file to be\n22\trevisited. The guards that closed B-1, B-2 and B-3 were inverted this way and\n23\tnow assert the fixed behaviour instead.\n24\t\n25\tSkips only where the hash-locked environment is absent; the node's evidence was\n26\tproduced by running this file inside it.\n27\t\"\"\"\n28\t\n29\timport ast\n30\timport hashlib\n31\timport inspect\n32\timport json\n33\timport random\n34\timport re\n35\timport sys\n36\timport tempfile\n37\timport unittest\n38\tfrom pathlib import Path\n39\tfrom typing import Any\n40\t\n41\ttry:  # pragma: no cover - environment probe, not behavior\n42\t    import langgraph  # noqa: F401\n43\t    import langgraph.checkpoint.sqlite  # noqa: F401\n44\texcept ModuleNotFoundError as exc:  # pragma: no cover\n45\t    raise unittest.SkipTest(\n46\t        \"plan26 hash-locked environment not installed \"\n47\t        \"(python3 -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/plan26.lock): \"\n48\t        f\"{exc}\"\n49\t    ) from exc\n50\t\n51\timport pytest\n52\timport yaml\n53\tfrom langgraph.channels.binop import BinaryOperatorAggregate\n54\tfrom langgraph.graph import END, START, StateGraph\n55\tfrom langgraph.types import Send\n56\tfrom typing_extensions import Annotated, TypedDict\n57\t\n58\tfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import graph as G\n59\tfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import model_nodes as mn\n60\tfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import persistence as P\n61\tfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import routing as R\n62\tfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import unit_graph as U\n63\tfrom runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes import (\n64\t    NODE_CATALOGUE,\n65\t    domain,\n66\t    inputs,\n67\t    render,\n68\t    review,\n69\t    sources,\n70\t    visuals,\n71\t)\n72\tfrom runtime.langgraph_factory.reducers import WriteOnceConflict, write_once\n73\tfrom runtime.langgraph_factory.state import (\n74\t    FACTORY_STATE_FIELDS,\n75\t    FIELD_REDUCER_CLASSES,\n76\t    FactoryState,\n77\t)\n78\t\n79\tREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n80\tUNIT_GRAPH_PY = REPO_ROOT / \"runtime\" / \"langgraph_factory\" / \"unit_graph.py\"\n81\t\n82\tMODEL_NODE_IDS = frozenset(mn.MODEL_NODE_ADAPTERS)\n83\t\n84\t\n85\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n86\t# fixtures — one real compiled graph, shared\n87\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n88\t\n89\t\n90\t@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\n91\tdef compiled() -> Any:\n92\t    output_root = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"plan26-n30-\"))\n93\t    return G.build_curriculum_factory_graph(engine_root=REPO_ROOT, output_root=output_root)\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\n97\tdef topology(compiled: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n98\t    return G.compiled_topology(compiled)\n99\t\n100\t\n101\t@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\n102\tdef available() -> tuple[str, ...]:\n103\t    return tuple(sorted(G.binding_inventory()))\n104\t\n105\t\n106\tclass _Token:\n107\t    def is_set(self) -> bool:\n108\t        return False\n109\t\n110\t\n111\tclass _Context:\n112\t    \"\"\"The narrow service surface a deterministic node body reaches.\"\"\"\n113\t\n114\t    def __init__(self, **services: Any) -> None:\n115\t        self.engine_root = services.pop(\"engine_root\", Path(\"/tmp\"))\n116\t        self.output_root = services.pop(\"output_root\", Path(\"/tmp/out\"))\n117\t        self.path_guard = object()\n118\t        self.evidence_service = object()\n119\t        self.transport_registry = services.pop(\"transport_registry\", object())\n120\t        self.source_retriever = services.pop(\"source_retriever\", None)\n121\t        self.signal_token = services.pop(\"signal_token\", _Token())\n122\t        self.clock = services.pop(\"clock\", lambda: \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\")\n123\t\n124\t\n125\tdef _sha256_file(path: Path) -> str:\n126\t    return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n127\t\n128\t\n129\tdef _synthetic_manifest(\n130\t    tmp_path: Path,\n131\t    unit_count: int,\n132\t    edges: dict[int, list[int]] | None = None,\n133\t    *,\n134\t    shuffle_seed: int | None = None,\n135\t) -> tuple[Path, list[str]]:\n136\t    \"\"\"A manifest of generically-named units over a chosen prerequisite DAG.\"\"\"\n137\t\n138\t    unit_ids = [f\"U{index:03d}\" for index in range(1, unit_count + 1)]\n139\t    units = []\n140\t    for index, unit_id in enumerate(unit_ids, start=1):\n141\t        prerequisites = [unit_ids[target - 1] for target in (edges or {}).get(index, [])]\n142\t        units.append(\n143\t            {\n144\t                \"id\": unit_id,\n145\t                \"title\": f\"synthetic unit {index}\",\n146\t                \"sequence\": {\"prerequisites\": prerequisites, \"prepares_for\": []},\n147\t                \"required_explanation\": [f\"fact {index}\"],\n148\t            }\n149\t        )\n150\t    if shuffle_seed is not None:\n151\t        random.Random(shuffle_seed).shuffle(units)\n152\t    curriculum_root = tmp_path / \"curricula\" / \"synthetic\"\n153\t    curriculum_root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n154\t    path = curriculum_root / \"synthetic_curriculum.v1.yaml\"\n155\t    path.write_text(yaml.safe_dump({\"labs\": units}, sort_keys=False), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n156\t    return path, [unit[\"id\"] for unit in units]\n157\t\n158\t\n159\tdef _d02_state(manifest_path: Path, mode: str, requested: str | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n160\t    return {\n161\t        \"engine_root\": str(manifest_path.parents[2]),\n162\t        \"curriculum_root\": str(manifest_path.parent),\n163\t        \"active_manifest_path\": str(manifest_path),\n164\t        \"mode\": mode,\n165\t        \"requested_unit_id\": requested,\n166\t        \"frozen_inputs\": [\n167\t            {\n168\t                \"path\": str(manifest_path),\n169\t                \"sha256\": _sha256_file(manifest_path),\n170\t                \"role\": \"active_manifest\",\n171\t            }\n172\t        ],\n173\t    }\n174\t\n175\t\n176\tdef _visual_state(\n177\t    unit_id: str,\n178\t    briefs: list[dict[str, Any]],\n179\t    results: dict[str, dict[str, Any]],\n180\t    *,\n181\t    content_hash: str = \"content-hash-1\",\n182\t) -> dict[str, Any]:\n183\t    \"\"\"A D12 projection over one frozen visual denominator.\n184\t\n185\t    `run_id`/`episode_id` are part of the projection because D12 stages an M04\n186\t    dispatch, and a dispatch with no run and episode identity has no correlation.\n187\t    \"\"\"\n188\t\n189\t    deterministic = sorted(b[\"key\"] for b in briefs if b[\"subset\"] == \"deterministic\")\n190\t    model = sorted(b[\"key\"] for b in briefs if b[\"subset\"] == \"model\")\n191\t    return {\n192\t        \"run_id\": \"run-n30-fixture\",\n193\t        \"episode_id\": \"episode-n30-fixture\",\n194\t        \"selected_unit_id\": unit_id,\n195\t        \"visual_briefs\": briefs,\n196\t        \"visual_denominators\": {\n197\t            f\"{unit_id}/{content_hash}\": {\n198\t                \"unit_id\": unit_id,\n199\t                \"content_hash\": content_hash,\n200\t                \"deterministic_keys\": deterministic,\n201\t                \"model_keys\": model,\n202\t                \"size\": len(briefs),\n203\t            }\n204\t        },\n205\t        \"visual_results\": results,\n206\t        \"artifact_versions\": [],\n207\t        \"artifact_heads\": {\n208\t            f\"units/{unit_id}/content\": {\"version\": 1, \"parent_hash\": None, \"hash\": content_hash}\n209\t        },\n210\t    }\n211\t\n212\t\n213\tdef _brief(unit_id: str, role: str, subset: str, content_hash: str = \"content-hash-1\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n214\t    return {\n215\t        \"key\": f\"{unit_id}/visual/{role}\",\n216\t        \"unit_id\": unit_id,\n217\t        \"role\": role,\n218\t        \"kind\": \"schematic\" if subset == \"deterministic\" else \"illustration\",\n219\t        \"subset\": subset,\n220\t        \"content_hash\": content_hash,\n221\t        \"domain_hash\": \"domain-hash-1\",\n222\t        \"permitted_facts\": [],\n223\t    }\n224\t\n225\t\n226\tdef _m02_packet(unit_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n227\t    \"\"\"One correctly reserved M02 packet, as D07 stages it and D90 restages it.\"\"\"\n228\t\n229\t    return {\n230\t        \"correlation\": {\"run_id\": \"r\", \"episode_id\": \"e\"},\n231\t        \"reservation\": {\n232\t            \"reservation_kind\": mn.RESERVATION_KIND,\n233\t            \"activation_id\": \"activation-1\",\n234\t            \"reservation_id\": \"activation-1#1\",\n235\t            \"job_id\": \"M02_CREATE_UNIT_DOMAIN_DATA\",\n236\t            \"counter_key\": \"M02_CREATE_UNIT_DOMAIN_DATA|k\",\n237\t            \"attempt_ordinal\": 1,\n238\t        },\n239\t        \"unit\": {\"unit_id\": unit_id, \"title\": \"t\"},\n240\t        \"admitted_sources\": [\n241\t            {\n242\t                \"source_id\": \"s1\",\n243\t                \"fact_id\": \"f1\",\n244\t                \"locator\": \"l\",\n245\t                \"sha256\": \"0\" * 64,\n246\t                \"content_type\": \"text/html\",\n247\t                \"scope\": \"required_explanation\",\n248\t            }\n249\t        ],\n250\t        \"domain_schema\": {\"path\": \"schemas/x.json\", \"sha256\": \"0\" * 64},\n251\t        \"verifier_interface\": {\"declared_at\": \"/verifier_result\"},\n252\t        \"calibration\": {\"path\": \"policy/x.yaml\", \"sha256\": \"0\" * 64},\n253\t    }\n254\t\n255\t\n256\tdef _visual_result(key: str, unit_id: str, subset: str, content_hash: str = \"content-hash-1\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n257\t    return {\n258\t        \"key\": key,\n259\t        \"unit_id\": unit_id,\n260\t        \"subset\": subset,\n261\t        \"provenance\": \"deterministic_renderer\" if subset == \"deterministic\" else \"model_candidate\",\n262\t        \"content_hash\": content_hash,\n263\t        \"domain_hash\": \"domain-hash-1\",\n264\t        \"asset_path\": f\"/tmp/{key}.svg\",\n265\t        \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(key.encode()).hexdigest(),\n266\t        \"format\": \"svg\",\n267\t    }\n268\t\n269\t\n270\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n271\t# End-to-end harness: the real compiled graph, a test-only model transport\n272\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n273\t#\n274\t# `RuntimeContext`'s services are opened by the CLI, not by the builder, so an\n275\t# episode can be executed against test doubles without changing production code.\n276\t# The one seam is the model transport: `graph._boundary` constructs it through\n277\t# `build_model_node_context`, which refuses a fake by design. The harness rebinds\n278\t# that one name for the duration of a test, so the fake stays unreachable from\n279\t# every production path (`test_the_model_path_uses_only_a_test_transport...`).\n280\t\n281\t\n282\tclass _StubRegistry:\n283\t    \"\"\"The capability/renderer/rasterizer surface D03/D11/D13/D14 reach for.\n284\t\n285\t    Production `CliTransport` implements none of these; see finding B-8.\n286\t    \"\"\"\n287\t\n288\t    def __init__(self, sandbox: Path) -> None:\n289\t        self.sandbox = sandbox\n290\t        self.rendered_units: list[str] = []\n291\t        self.inspected: list[str] = []\n292\t\n293\t    def prove_capability(self, capability: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n294\t        return {\"result\": \"PASS\", \"capability\": capability, \"detail\": \"test double\"}\n295\t\n296\t    def observe_executable(self, name: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n297\t        return {\"name\": name, \"path\": f\"/usr/bin/{name}\", \"sha256\": \"0\" * 64}\n298\t\n299\t    def render_deterministic_visual(self, brief: Any, permitted_facts: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n300\t        path = self.sandbox / \"visuals\" / (str(brief[\"key\"]).replace(\"/\", \"_\") + \".svg\")\n301\t        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n302\t        body = f\"<svg data-key='{brief['key']}'/>\".encode()\n303\t        path.write_bytes(body)\n304\t        return {\"asset_path\": str(path), \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(body).hexdigest(), \"format\": \"svg\"}\n305\t\n306\t    def render_unit(self, unit_id: str, parents: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n307\t        self.rendered_units.append(unit_id)\n308\t        directory = self.sandbox / \"render\"\n309\t        directory.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n310\t        body = json.dumps({\"unit\": unit_id, \"parents\": parents}, sort_keys=True).encode()\n311\t        pdf, layout = directory / f\"{unit_id}.pdf\", directory / f\"{unit_id}.layout.json\"\n312\t        pdf.write_bytes(body)\n313\t        layout.write_bytes(body)\n314\t        digest = hashlib.sha256(body).hexdigest()\n315\t        return {\n316\t            \"layout_path\": str(layout),\n317\t            \"layout_sha256\": digest,\n318\t            \"pdf_path\": str(pdf),\n319\t            \"pdf_sha256\": digest,\n320\t            \"renderer\": \"test_double_renderer\",\n321\t            \"attempt\": 1,\n322\t        }\n323\t\n324\t    def inspect_pages(self, pdf_path: str, pdf_sha256: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n325\t        self.inspected.append(pdf_sha256)\n326\t        pages = []\n327\t        for number in (1, 2):\n328\t            image = self.sandbox / \"pages\" / f\"{Path(pdf_path).stem}-{number}.png\"\n329\t            image.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n330\t            body = f\"page-{number}-{pdf_sha256}\".encode()\n331\t            image.write_bytes(body)\n332\t            pages.append(\n333\t                {\n334\t                    \"number\": number,\n335\t                    \"page_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(body).hexdigest(),\n336\t                    \"image_path\": str(image),\n337\t                    \"problems\": [],\n338\t                    \"unreadable\": False,\n339\t                }\n340\t            )\n341\t        return {\"pages\": pages}\n342\t\n343\t\n344\tclass _StubRetriever:\n345\t    def __init__(self) -> None:\n346\t        self.fetched: list[str] = []\n347\t\n348\t    def fetch(self, locator: Any, authorization: Any, scope: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n349\t        self.fetched.append(str(locator))\n350\t        body = json.dumps({\"locator\": locator, \"scope\": scope}, sort_keys=True).encode()\n351\t        return {\n352\t            \"locator\": locator,\n353\t            \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(body).hexdigest(),\n354\t            \"status\": 200,\n355\t            \"content_type\": \"text/html\",\n356\t            \"tls\": {\"verified\": True},\n357\t            \"bytes_path\": None,\n358\t        }\n359\t\n360\t\n361\tclass _SwitchableToken:\n362\t    \"\"\"A signal token a test can raise at a chosen node boundary.\"\"\"\n363\t\n364\t    def __init__(self, trip_after: str | None = None) -> None:\n365\t        self.trip_after = trip_after\n366\t        self.tripped = False\n367\t        self.observed: list[str] = []\n368\t\n369\t    def trip(self) -> None:\n370\t        self.tripped = True\n371\t\n372\t    def is_set(self) -> bool:\n373\t        return self.tripped\n374\t\n375\t\n376\tclass _HarnessContext:\n377\t    \"\"\"`RuntimeContext`-shaped test double. No product root, no real transport.\"\"\"\n378\t\n379\t    def __init__(self, engine_root: Path, output_root: Path, sandbox: Path) -> None:\n380\t        from runtime.langgraph_factory.artifacts import ArtifactStore\n381\t        from runtime.langgraph_factory.evidence import EvidenceStore\n382\t\n383\t        self.engine_root = engine_root\n384\t        self.output_root = output_root\n385\t        self.path_guard = ArtifactStore(output_root)\n386\t        self.evidence_service = EvidenceStore(output_root)\n387\t        self.transport_registry = _StubRegistry(sandbox)\n388\t        self.source_retriever = _StubRetriever()\n389\t        self.signal_token = _SwitchableToken()\n390\t        self.clock = lambda: \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\"\n391\t\n392\t\n393\tclass _ScriptedFakeTransport(mn.tp.FakeCliTransport):\n394\t    \"\"\"Composes each canned candidate from the projection it is handed.\n395\t\n396\t    Still a `FakeCliTransport`, so the real output-schema and no-authoritative-\n397\t    field validation still runs, and it is still refused by\n398\t    `build_model_node_context`.\n399\t    \"\"\"\n400\t\n401\t    def __init__(self, *, sandbox_root: Path, registry: Any = None) -> None:\n402\t        super().__init__(sandbox_root=sandbox_root, responses={}, registry=registry)\n403\t        self.calls: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n404\t\n405\t    def execute(self, *, job_id: str, activation_id: str, projection: Any = None, **kwargs: Any):\n406\t        projection = dict(projection or {})\n407\t        self.calls.append((job_id, activation_id))\n408\t        self.responses[job_id] = _scripted_candidate(job_id, projection)\n409\t        return super().execute(\n410\t            job_id=job_id, activation_id=activation_id, projection=projection, **kwargs\n411\t        )\n412\t\n413\t\n414\t# The visual denominator the scripted M03 declares. Two members, one per subset,\n415\t# so a real episode fans out to D11 *and* to M04 and D12 has two subsets to join.\n416\t# `_declared_visuals` returns the list in a chosen order, which is what prompt\n417\t# TEST 5's permutation-invariance claim varies.\n418\tDECLARED_VISUALS: list[dict[str, Any]] = [\n419\t    {\n420\t        \"role\": \"build_map\",\n421\t        \"kind\": \"schematic\",\n422\t        \"authoritative\": True,\n423\t        \"permitted_facts\": [\"fact-a\"],\n424\t    },\n425\t    {\n426\t        \"role\": \"overview\",\n427\t        \"kind\": \"diagram\",\n428\t        \"authoritative\": False,\n429\t        \"permitted_facts\": [\"fact-b\"],\n430\t    },\n431\t]\n432\t\n433\t\n434\tdef _scripted_candidate(job_id: str, projection: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n435\t    if job_id == \"M01_RESEARCH_UNIT_SOURCES\":\n436\t        request_id = projection[\"request\"].get(\"request_id\")\n437\t        group = projection.get(\"retrieval_group\")\n438\t        if group is None:\n439\t            return {\n440\t                \"locators\": [\n441\t                    {\n442\t                        \"request_id\": request_id,\n443\t                        \"url\": f\"https://example.invalid/{request_id}\",\n444\t                        \"title\": \"scripted source\",\n445\t                        \"publisher\": \"scripted publisher\",\n446\t                        \"locator_kind\": \"primary\",\n447\t                        \"rationale\": \"scripted rationale\",\n448\t                    }\n449\t                ]\n450\t            }\n451\t        return {\n452\t            \"interpretations\": [\n453\t                {\n454\t                    \"request_id\": request_id,\n455\t                    \"retrieval_id\": str(record.get(\"retrieval_id\")),\n456\t                    \"claims\": [\n457\t                        {\n458\t                            \"claim_text\": \"scripted claim\",\n459\t                            \"source_quote\": \"scripted quote\",\n460\t                            \"source_location\": \"p.1\",\n461\t                        }\n462\t                    ],\n463\t                    \"limitations\": [],\n464\t                }\n465\t                for record in group.get(\"retrieved_records\", [])\n466\t            ]\n467\t        }\n468\t    if job_id == \"M02_CREATE_UNIT_DOMAIN_DATA\":\n469\t        unit_id = projection[\"unit\"].get(\"unit_id\")\n470\t        admitted = projection.get(\"admitted_sources\") or []\n471\t        # Every declared fact resolves to an admitted source, which is D08's\n472\t        # `domain_facts_sourced` check: the body is derived from the join, not\n473\t        # invented alongside it.\n474\t        facts = [\n475\t            {\n476\t                \"fact_id\": str(source.get(\"fact_id\")),\n477\t                \"statement\": f\"scripted statement for {source.get('fact_id')}\",\n478\t            }\n479\t            for source in admitted\n480\t        ] or [{\"fact_id\": \"required_explanation:000\", \"statement\": \"scripted statement\"}]\n481\t        return {\n482\t            \"domain_version\": {\n483\t                \"unit_id\": unit_id,\n484\t                \"fields\": {\n485\t                    \"unit_id\": unit_id,\n486\t                    \"facts\": facts,\n487\t                    \"verifier_result\": {\"result\": \"all_fixtures_behaved\"},\n488\t                },\n489\t                \"evidence_references\": [\n490\t                    {\n491\t                        \"source_id\": str(source.get(\"source_id\") or source.get(\"key\") or \"s1\"),\n492\t                        \"source_location\": \"p.1\",\n493\t                    }\n494\t                    for source in admitted\n495\t                ]\n496\t                or [{\"source_id\": \"s1\", \"source_location\": \"p.1\"}],\n497\t            }\n498\t        }\n499\t    if job_id == \"M03_WRITE_UNIT_CONTENT\":\n500\t        admitted_domain = projection.get(\"admitted_domain\") or {}\n501\t        unit_id = str(admitted_domain.get(\"unit_id\") or projection[\"unit\"].get(\"unit_id\"))\n502\t        # Only the source ids D08 declared admissible may be cited; M03's adapter\n503\t        # rejects any other as `candidate_undeclared_artifact`.\n504\t        admissible = projection.get(\"admitted_evidence_references\") or []\n505\t        return {\n506\t            \"unit_content\": {\n507\t                \"unit_id\": unit_id,\n508\t                \"sections\": [\n509\t                    {\n510\t                        \"section_id\": f\"s{index:03d}\",\n511\t                        \"heading\": f\"scripted heading {index}\",\n512\t                        \"body\": f\"scripted body for {reference.get('fact_id')}\",\n513\t                    }\n514\t                    for index, reference in enumerate(admissible, start=1)\n515\t                ],\n516\t                \"evidence_references\": [\n517\t                    {\n518\t                        \"section_id\": f\"s{index:03d}\",\n519\t                        \"source_id\": str(reference.get(\"source_id\")),\n520\t                        \"source_location\": \"p.1\",\n521\t                    }\n522\t                    for index, reference in enumerate(admissible, start=1)\n523\t                ],\n524\t                # One visual of each subset, so the episode exercises both halves\n525\t                # of D12's join: `schematic` is in `AUTHORITATIVE_VISUAL_KINDS`\n526\t                # and is produced deterministically from the domain, `diagram` is\n527\t                # not and is dispatched to M04.\n528\t                \"visuals\": DECLARED_VISUALS,\n529\t            }\n530\t        }\n531\t    if job_id == \"M04_CREATE_UNIT_VISUALS\":\n532\t        brief_id = str(projection[\"brief\"].get(\"brief_id\") or projection[\"brief\"].get(\"key\"))\n533\t        return {\n534\t            \"visual_candidate\": {\n535\t                \"brief_id\": brief_id,\n536\t                \"prompt_text\": f\"scripted prompt for {brief_id}\",\n537\t                \"dimensions\": {\"width_px\": 1024, \"height_px\": 768},\n538\t                \"image_format\": \"png\",\n539\t                \"accessibility_text\": f\"scripted alt text for {brief_id}\",\n540\t            },\n541\t            \"provenance_declaration\": {\n542\t                \"brief_id\": brief_id,\n543\t                \"permitted_facts_used\": [\n544\t                    str(fact) for fact in (projection.get(\"permitted_facts\") or [])\n545\t                ],\n546\t                \"asserts_authoritative_detail\": False,\n547\t            },\n548\t        }\n549\t    if job_id == \"M05_REVIEW_ACTUAL_UNIT\":\n550\t        # The review answers the exact page denominator D15 froze, by hash: a\n551\t        # review that invented or dropped a page is what D16's join exists to\n552\t        # reject, so the scripted reviewer must not do either.\n553\t        pages = projection.get(\"pages\") or []\n554\t        return {\n555\t            \"overall_findings\": [],\n556\t            \"page_findings\": [\n557\t                {\n558\t                    \"page_number\": int(page[\"page_number\"]),\n559\t                    \"page_sha256\": str(page[\"page_sha256\"]),\n560\t                    \"findings\": [],\n561\t                }\n562\t                for page in pages\n563\t            ],\n564\t        }\n565\t    raise AssertionError(f\"no scripted candidate for {job_id}\")\n566\t\n567\t\n568\tdef _scripted_model_context(sandbox: Path) -> Any:\n569\t    routes = mn.tp.load_job_registry()\n570\t    return mn.ModelNodeContext(\n571\t        transport=_ScriptedFakeTransport(sandbox_root=sandbox, registry=routes),\n572\t        registry=routes,\n573\t    )\n574\t\n575\t\n576\t# The engine contracts the unit path resolves out of its engine root. D07 hands\n577\t# the domain metaschema and calibration to M02, D08 loads the run's domain schema,\n578\t# and D09 holds unit content to `CURRICULUM_CONTRACTS[0]`. They are copied from the\n579\t# repo rather than stubbed, so the episode is held to the contracts a real run is.\n580\tENGINE_CONTRACTS: tuple[str, ...] = (\n581\t    \"schemas/manifest_domain.metaschema.v1.json\",\n582\t    \"policy/calibration.v1.yaml\",\n583\t    \"meta_prompt/assets/pedagogy.v1.md\",\n584\t    *domain.CURRICULUM_CONTRACTS,\n585\t)\n586\t\n587\t# The synthetic curriculum's own declared domain contract. A run that declares one\n588\t# is the path D02/D08 are built for; the engine metaschema constrains the shape of\n589\t# *this* file, not the domain instance a unit asserts.\n590\tSYNTHETIC_DOMAIN_SCHEMA_RELATIVE = \"schemas/synthetic_domain.v1.json\"\n591\tSYNTHETIC_DOMAIN_SCHEMA: dict[str, Any] = {\n592\t    \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n593\t    \"$id\": \"plan26/test/synthetic_domain.v1.json\",\n594\t    \"type\": \"object\",\n595\t    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n596\t    \"required\": [\"unit_id\", \"facts\", \"verifier_result\"],\n597\t    \"properties\": {\n598\t        \"unit_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n599\t        \"facts\": {\n600\t            \"type\": \"array\",\n601\t            \"minItems\": 1,\n602\t            \"items\": {\n603\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n604\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n605\t                \"required\": [\"fact_id\", \"statement\"],\n606\t                \"properties\": {\n607\t                    \"fact_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n608\t                    \"statement\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n609\t                },\n610\t            },\n611\t        },\n612\t        \"verifier_result\": {\n613\t            \"type\": \"object\",\n614\t            \"additionalProperties\": True,\n615\t            \"required\": [\"result\"],\n616\t            \"properties\": {\"result\": {\"type\": \"string\"}},\n617\t        },\n618\t    },\n619\t}\n620\t\n621\t\n622\tdef _build_episode_fixture(tmp_path: Path, units: int = 1) -> dict[str, Any]:\n623\t    \"\"\"An engine root, a synthetic curriculum, an output root, and a sandbox.\"\"\"\n624\t\n625\t    engine = tmp_path / \"engine\"\n626\t    curriculum = engine / \"curricula\" / \"synthetic\"\n627\t    curriculum.mkdir(parents=True)\n628\t    for name in (\"schemas\", \"policy\", \"meta_prompt\"):\n629\t        (engine / name).mkdir()\n630\t    (engine / \"schemas\" / \"placeholder.json\").write_text(\"{}\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n631\t    for relative in ENGINE_CONTRACTS:\n632\t        target = engine / relative\n633\t        target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n634\t        target.write_bytes((REPO_ROOT / relative).read_bytes())\n635\t    (engine / SYNTHETIC_DOMAIN_SCHEMA_RELATIVE).write_text(\n636\t        json.dumps(SYNTHETIC_DOMAIN_SCHEMA, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\"\n637\t    )\n638\t    labs = [\n639\t        {\n640\t            \"id\": f\"U{index:03d}\",\n641\t            \"title\": f\"synthetic unit {index}\",\n642\t            \"sequence\": {\n643\t                \"prerequisites\": [f\"U{index - 1:03d}\"] if index > 1 else [],\n644\t                \"prepares_for\": [],\n645\t            },\n646\t            \"required_explanation\": [f\"fact {index}\"],\n647\t            \"safety_focus\": [\"care\"],\n648\t        }\n649\t        for index in range(1, units + 1)\n650\t    ]\n651\t    manifest = curriculum / \"synthetic_curriculum.v1.yaml\"\n652\t    manifest.write_text(\n653\t        yaml.safe_dump(\n654\t            {\n655\t                \"domain\": {\"manifest_schema\": SYNTHETIC_DOMAIN_SCHEMA_RELATIVE},\n656\t                \"labs\": labs,\n657\t            },\n658\t            sort_keys=False,\n659\t        ),\n660\t        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n661\t    )\n662\t    output_root = tmp_path / \"out\"\n663\t    output_root.mkdir()\n664\t    # The fake transport refuses any root that is not under the system temp dir.\n665\t    sandbox = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"plan26-n30-sandbox-\"))\n666\t    return {\n667\t        \"engine\": engine,\n668\t        \"curriculum\": curriculum,\n669\t        \"manifest\": manifest,\n670\t        \"output_root\": output_root,\n671\t        \"sandbox\": sandbox,\n672\t    }\n673\t\n674\t\n675\tdef _prepare_episode(fixture: dict[str, Any], *, mode: str = \"one\", requested: str | None = \"U001\"):\n676\t    \"\"\"`prepare_episode_invocation` plus the envelope D00 reads, as the CLI builds them.\"\"\"\n677\t\n678\t    lock = P.ExecutionLock(fixture[\"output_root\"])\n679\t    lock.acquire()\n680\t    seed = {\n681\t        \"engine_root\": str(fixture[\"engine\"]),\n682\t        \"curriculum_root\": str(fixture[\"curriculum\"]),\n683\t        \"active_manifest_path\": str(fixture[\"manifest\"]),\n684\t        \"output_root\": str(fixture[\"output_root\"]),\n685\t        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\n686\t        \"contract_version\": \"1\",\n687\t        \"mode\": mode,\n688\t        \"requested_unit_id\": requested,\n689\t    }\n690\t    invocation = P.prepare_episode_invocation(\n691\t        output_root=fixture[\"output_root\"], lock=lock, identity_seed=seed\n692\t    )\n693\t    envelope: dict[str, Any] = {\n694\t        \"kind\": \"fresh\",\n695\t        \"contract_version\": \"1\",\n696\t        \"engine_root\": str(fixture[\"engine\"]),\n697\t        \"curriculum_root\": str(fixture[\"curriculum\"]),\n698\t        \"output_root\": str(fixture[\"output_root\"]),\n699\t        \"mode\": mode,\n700\t        \"requested_unit_id\": requested,\n701\t        \"authorization\": {\"scope\": \"test\", \"executables\": []},\n702\t        \"episode_ordinal\": 1,\n703\t        \"prior_identity\": None,\n704\t        \"prior_terminal\": None,\n705\t        \"lease_open\": False,\n706\t    }\n707\t    # D03 requires the authorization to name this run's frozen digest, which the\n708\t    # CLI computes before invocation; D01 is the one function that derives it.\n709\t    probe = _HarnessContext(fixture[\"engine\"], fixture[\"output_root\"], fixture[\"sandbox\"])\n710\t    digest = inputs.D01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS({\"invocation\": envelope}, probe)[\"frozen_digest\"]\n711\t    envelope[\"authorization\"] = {\n712\t        \"scope\": \"test\",\n713\t        \"executables\": [],\n714\t        \"curriculum_digest\": digest,\n715\t    }\n716\t    return lock, invocation, envelope\n717\t\n718\t\n719\tdef _run_episode(\n720\t    monkeypatch: Any,\n721\t    fixture: dict[str, Any],\n722\t    *,\n723\t    interrupt_after: str | None = None,\n724\t) -> dict[str, Any]:\n725\t    \"\"\"Execute one real episode of the real compiled graph, end to end.\n726\t\n727\t    Returns the ordered node trace, the per-node updates, and the final state.\n728\t    \"\"\"\n729\t\n730\t    lock, invocation, envelope = _prepare_episode(fixture)\n731\t    context = _HarnessContext(fixture[\"engine\"], fixture[\"output_root\"], fixture[\"sandbox\"])\n732\t    monkeypatch.setattr(\n733\t        G,\n734\t        \"build_model_node_context\",\n735\t        lambda _context, **_kwargs: _scripted_model_context(fixture[\"sandbox\"]),\n736\t    )\n737\t    compiled = G.build_curriculum_factory_graph(\n738\t        engine_root=fixture[\"engine\"], output_root=fixture[\"output_root\"]\n739\t    )\n740\t\n741\t    trace: list[str] = []\n742\t    updates: list[tuple[str, dict[str, Any]]] = []\n743\t    deferred_frontier: str | None = None\n744\t    try:\n745\t        for chunk in compiled.stream(\n746\t            {\"invocation\": envelope},\n747\t            config=invocation.config,\n748\t            stream_mode=\"updates\",\n749\t            context=context,\n750\t        ):\n751\t            for node_id, update in chunk.items():\n752\t                trace.append(node_id)\n753\t                updates.append((node_id, dict(update or {})))\n754\t                if interrupt_after is not None and node_id == interrupt_after:\n755\t                    context.signal_token.trip()\n756\t    except KeyError as error:\n757\t        # A guard resolved a destination whose node body does not exist yet.\n758\t        # That is a *declared* deferred edge, not a defect, so it is recorded as\n759\t        # the episode's frontier — but only if it really is one of the declared\n760\t        # rows, so an undeclared missing destination still fails loudly.\n761\t        missing = error.args[0] if error.args else None\n762\t        declared = {row[2] for row in U.DEFERRED_EDGES}\n763\t        if missing not in declared:\n764\t            raise\n765\t        deferred_frontier = str(missing)\n766\t    lock.release()\n767\t    return {\n768\t        \"trace\": trace,\n769\t        \"updates\": updates,\n770\t        \"deferred_frontier\": deferred_frontier,\n771\t        \"state\": compiled.get_state(invocation.config).values,\n772\t        \"context\": context,\n773\t        \"invocation\": invocation,\n774\t        \"compiled\": compiled,\n775\t    }\n776\t\n777\t\n778\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n779\t# Registered unit topology (spec 8.1 / 8.2)\n780\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n781\t\n782\t\n783\tdef test_the_compiled_graph_registers_every_declared_unit_branch(topology, available) -> None:\n784\t    \"\"\"Each conditional edge exists with exactly the destinations that exist.\"\"\"\n785\t\n786\t    registered: dict[str, set[str]] = {}\n787\t    for source, target, conditional in topology[\"edges\"]:\n788\t        if conditional:\n789\t            registered.setdefault(source, set()).add(target)\n790\t\n791\t    for source, _guard in U.UNIT_BRANCHES:\n792\t        expected = set(U.branch_destinations(source, available))\n793\t        assert expected, f\"{source} has no registerable destination\"\n794\t        assert registered.get(source) == expected, source\n795\t\n796\t\n797\tdef test_the_two_map_reduce_return_edges_are_normal_edges(topology) -> None:\n798\t    \"\"\"Spec 8.2 names these exactly: `add_edge(worker, barrier)`, not a branch.\n799\t\n800\t    Registering the worker's return conditionally would let the worker's own\n801\t    result decide where the map/reduce goes, which is the barrier's authority.\n802\t    \"\"\"\n803\t\n804\t    normal = {(source, target) for source, target, conditional in topology[\"edges\"] if not conditional}\n805\t    for edge in U.UNIT_NORMAL_EDGES:\n806\t        assert edge in normal, edge\n807\t    assert (\"D11_CREATE_DETERMINISTIC_VISUALS\", \"D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN\") in normal\n808\t    assert (\"M04_CREATE_UNIT_VISUALS\", \"D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN\") in normal\n809\t\n810\t\n811\tdef test_the_unit_path_creates_no_second_graph_and_compiles_nothing() -> None:\n812\t    \"\"\"N30 is additive registration over N20's one builder.\"\"\"\n813\t\n814\t    source = UNIT_GRAPH_PY.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n815\t    tree = ast.parse(source)\n816\t    calls = [\n817\t        node.func.id if isinstance(node.func, ast.Name) else getattr(node.func, \"attr\", \"\")\n818\t        for node in ast.walk(tree)\n819\t        if isinstance(node, ast.Call)\n820\t    ]\n821\t    assert \"StateGraph\" not in calls\n822\t    assert \"compile\" not in calls\n823\t    assert \"add_node\" not in calls\n824\t\n825\t\n826\tdef test_a_node_body_authored_in_the_unit_path_module_is_refused() -> None:\n827\t    \"\"\"The D90/D91 gap cannot be closed by writing a wrapper in this module.\n828\t\n829\t    N20's `validate_bindings` restricts a production binding to the two owned\n830\t    node modules, so a callable authored here is rejected by stable ID. This is\n831\t    why blocking gap `plan26/n30/d90-d91-not-registrable` is owed to N23 and\n832\t    cannot be absorbed as coordination.\n833\t    \"\"\"\n834\t\n835\t    def D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT(state: Any, context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n836\t        return {}\n837\t\n838\t    D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT.__module__ = \"runtime.langgraph_factory.unit_graph\"\n839\t    bindings = dict(G.binding_inventory())\n840\t    bindings[\"D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT\"] = D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT\n841\t\n842\t    with pytest.raises(G.GraphBindingError) as error:\n843\t        G.validate_bindings(bindings, required=(\"D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT\",))\n844\t    assert \"N20-BIND-PLACEHOLDER\" in str(error.value)\n845\t\n846\t\n847\tdef test_deferred_edges_are_exactly_the_destinations_with_no_node_body(available) -> None:\n848\t    \"\"\"Silence about an unwireable edge is how a topology gap becomes a halt.\"\"\"\n849\t\n850\t    observed: set[tuple[str, str]] = set()\n851\t    for source, _guard in U.UNIT_BRANCHES:\n852\t        for destination in U.deferred_destinations(source, available):\n853\t            observed.add((source, destination))\n854\t    declared = {(source, destination) for source, _value, destination, _owner in U.DEFERRED_EDGES}\n855\t    assert observed == declared\n856\t\n857\t\n858\tdef test_every_deferred_edge_names_a_real_owning_graph_node() -> None:\n859\t    owners = {owner for _s, _v, _d, owner in U.DEFERRED_EDGES}\n860\t    assert owners <= {\"N23_MODEL_NODES\", \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\", \"N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS\"}\n861\t    for _source, value, destination, owner in U.DEFERRED_EDGES:\n862\t        assert value and destination and owner\n863\t\n864\t\n865\tdef test_registering_an_undeclared_deferred_destination_fails(monkeypatch, available) -> None:\n866\t    \"\"\"A future unwireable destination must be declared, not silently dropped.\"\"\"\n867\t\n868\t    monkeypatch.setattr(U, \"DEFERRED_EDGES\", U.DEFERRED_EDGES[1:])\n869\t\n870\t    class _Builder:\n871\t        def add_edge(self, *args: Any) -> None:\n872\t            pass\n873\t\n874\t        def add_conditional_edges(self, *args: Any) -> None:\n875\t            pass\n876\t\n877\t    with pytest.raises(U.UnitTopologyError) as error:\n878\t        U.register_unit_path(_Builder(), available)\n879\t    assert \"N30-EDGE-UNDECLARED\" in str(error.value)\n880\t\n881\t\n882\tdef test_no_model_node_can_be_a_resume_reentry_destination(topology) -> None:\n883\t    \"\"\"Spec 6.2 D92: a model node as stored destination is a system failure.\"\"\"\n884\t\n885\t    assert not set(U.RESUME_REENTRY_DESTINATIONS) & MODEL_NODE_IDS\n886\t    reentry = {\n887\t        target\n888\t        for source, target, conditional in topology[\"edges\"]\n889\t        if source == \"D92_REENTER_VALIDATED_FRONTIER\" and conditional\n890\t    }\n891\t    assert not reentry & MODEL_NODE_IDS\n892\t    assert set(U.RESUME_REENTRY_DESTINATIONS) <= reentry\n893\t\n894\t\n895\tdef test_a_stored_model_frontier_is_refused_by_the_reentry_guard() -> None:\n896\t    state = {\n897\t        \"pending_guard\": {\n898\t            \"node\": \"D92_REENTER_VALIDATED_FRONTIER\",\n899\t            \"value\": \"deterministic_reentry\",\n900\t            \"detail\": {\"destination\": \"M03_WRITE_UNIT_CONTENT\"},\n901\t        }\n902\t    }\n903\t    with pytest.raises(R.RoutingViolation):\n904\t        R.route_frontier_reentry(state)\n905\t\n906\t\n907\tdef test_the_unit_path_names_no_unit_id_and_no_manifest_length() -> None:\n908\t    \"\"\"Spec 8.2: the builder never creates a node per known unit.\"\"\"\n909\t\n910\t    source = UNIT_GRAPH_PY.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n911\t    tree = ast.parse(source)\n912\t    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n913\t        if isinstance(node, ast.Constant) and isinstance(node.value, int):\n914\t            assert node.value in (0, 1), f\"manifest-length-looking constant {node.value}\"\n915\t    assert \"U001\" not in source\n916\t\n917\t\n918\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n919\t# Fan-outs, denominators, joins (spec section 10)\n920\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n921\t\n922\t\n923\tdef test_a_visual_fanout_dispatches_one_send_per_staged_denominator_member() -> None:\n924\t    \"\"\"The guard translates staged material one-for-one; it invents no member.\n925\t\n926\t    Since N20's B-6 rework the dispatcher no longer emits the `Send`s itself: a\n927\t    model fan-out routes to D90, D90 commits one attempt counter per member and\n928\t    restages the packet, and `route_attempt_reservation` is the guard that turns\n929\t    the *reserved* members into `Send`s. The one-for-one property is asserted\n930\t    across that hop, so the members dispatched are still exactly the members the\n931\t    denominator committed to — each now additionally carrying its reservation.\n932\t    \"\"\"\n933\t\n934\t    unit_id = \"U001\"\n935\t    briefs = [\n936\t        _brief(unit_id, \"det-a\", \"deterministic\"),\n937\t        _brief(unit_id, \"mdl-a\", \"model\"),\n938\t        _brief(unit_id, \"mdl-b\", \"model\"),\n939\t    ]\n940\t    results = {\n941\t        f\"{unit_id}/visual/det-a\": _visual_result(f\"{unit_id}/visual/det-a\", unit_id, \"deterministic\")\n942\t    }\n943\t    state = _visual_state(unit_id, briefs, results)\n944\t    update = visuals.D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN(state, _Context())\n945\t\n946\t    assert update[\"pending_guard\"][\"value\"] == \"model_visual_fanout\"\n947\t    packet = update[\"pending_packet\"]\n948\t    assert packet[\"dispatch\"] == \"M04_CREATE_UNIT_VISUALS\"\n949\t    members = packet[\"packets\"]\n950\t    assert len(members) == 2\n951\t    # Each member is an M04 packet, not a bare brief: `Send` delivers the member\n952\t    # as the worker's whole input, so it has to carry the spec 9 projection.\n953\t    for member in members:\n954\t        assert set(member) >= {\"brief\", \"permitted_facts\", \"visual_contract\", \"correlation\"}\n955\t        assert member[\"correlation\"][\"run_id\"] == state[\"run_id\"]\n956\t        assert member[\"correlation\"][\"episode_id\"] == state[\"episode_id\"]\n957\t\n958\t    # The dispatcher's own guard reserves before it dispatches (spec 6.2, D90).\n959\t    assert R.route_visual_barrier({**state, **update}) == \"D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT\"\n960\t\n961\t    reserved = mn.D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT({**state, **update}, None)\n962\t    restaged = reserved[\"pending_packet\"][\"packets\"]\n963\t    assert len(restaged) == 2\n964\t\n965\t    dispatch = R.route_attempt_reservation({**state, **update, **reserved})\n966\t    assert isinstance(dispatch, list) and len(dispatch) == 2\n967\t    assert all(isinstance(send, Send) for send in dispatch)\n968\t    assert {send.node for send in dispatch} == {\"M04_CREATE_UNIT_VISUALS\"}\n969\t    assert [send.arg for send in dispatch] == restaged\n970\t    # One `Send` per committed denominator member, and each carries the counter\n971\t    # that was committed for it and nothing invented at routing time.\n972\t    assert [send.arg[\"correlation\"][\"correlation_key\"] for send in dispatch] == [\n973\t        member[\"correlation\"][\"correlation_key\"] for member in members\n974\t    ]\n975\t    assert len({send.arg[\"reservation\"][\"activation_id\"] for send in dispatch}) == 2\n976\t\n977\t\n978\tdef test_a_fanout_with_no_staged_packet_refuses_to_improvise_one() -> None:\n979\t    \"\"\"Spec 10: the denominator is persisted before dispatch, not at routing time.\n980\t\n981\t    The refusal lives wherever a guard actually translates members into `Send`s.\n982\t    Since B-6 that is two places: D10's deterministic map still translates at the\n983\t    dispatcher, and every model map translates at D90. Both are asserted, so\n984\t    moving the dispatch hop did not move the property out of the file.\n985\t    \"\"\"\n986\t\n987\t    model_dispatch = {\n988\t        \"pending_guard\": {\n989\t            \"node\": \"D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT\",\n990\t            \"value\": \"authorized\",\n991\t            \"kind\": \"model_attempt\",\n992\t            \"decision\": \"authorized\",\n993\t            \"detail\": {},\n994\t        }\n995\t    }\n996\t    with pytest.raises(R.RoutingViolation):\n997\t        R.route_attempt_reservation(model_dispatch)\n998\t\n999\t    deterministic_dispatch = {\n1000\t        \"pending_guard\": {\n1001\t            \"node\": \"D10_COMPILE_VISUAL_BRIEFS\",\n1002\t            \"value\": \"deterministic_visual_fanout\",\n1003\t            \"detail\": {},\n1004\t        }\n1005\t    }\n1006\t    with pytest.raises(R.RoutingViolation):\n1007\t        R.route_visual_briefs(deterministic_dispatch)\n1008\t\n1009\t\n1010\tdef test_an_empty_deterministic_visual_subset_routes_straight_to_the_barrier() -> None:\n1011\t    \"\"\"Spec 8.2: empty subsets route directly through D12; no sentinel member.\"\"\"\n1012\t\n1013\t    unit_id = \"U001\"\n1014\t    content_hash = \"content-hash-1\"\n1015\t    state = {\n1016\t        \"selected_unit_id\": unit_id,\n1017\t        \"artifact_heads\": {\n1018\t            f\"units/{unit_id}/content\": {\"version\": 1, \"parent_hash\": None, \"hash\": content_hash},\n1019\t            f\"units/{unit_id}/domain\": {\"version\": 1, \"parent_hash\": None, \"hash\": \"domain-hash-1\"},\n1020\t        },\n1021\t        \"artifact_versions\": [\n1022\t            {\n1023\t                \"stream\": f\"units/{unit_id}/content\",\n1024\t                \"version\": 1,\n1025\t                \"parent_hash\": None,\n1026\t                \"hash\": content_hash,\n1027\t                \"body\": {\"visuals\": [{\"role\": \"mdl-a\", \"kind\": \"illustration\"}]},\n1028\t            }\n1029\t        ],\n1030\t        \"engine_root\": \"/tmp\",\n1031\t    }\n1032\t    update = visuals.D10_COMPILE_VISUAL_BRIEFS(state, _Context())\n1033\t    assert update[\"pending_guard\"][\"value\"] == \"no_deterministic_visuals\"\n1034\t    assert R.route_visual_briefs({**state, **update}) == \"D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN\"\n1035\t\n1036\t\n1037\t@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n1038\t    \"mutation\",\n1039\t    [\"missing\", \"extra\", \"stale_parent\", \"cross_unit\"],\n1040\t)\n1041\tdef test_the_visual_join_refuses_a_denominator_that_is_not_exact(mutation: str) -> None:\n1042\t    \"\"\"Spec 10: missing, extra, stale-parent and cross-unit members fail the join.\"\"\"\n1043\t\n1044\t    unit_id = \"U001\"\n1045\t    briefs = [_brief(unit_id, \"det-a\", \"deterministic\"), _brief(unit_id, \"det-b\", \"deterministic\")]\n1046\t    key_a, key_b = f\"{unit_id}/visual/det-a\", f\"{unit_id}/visual/det-b\"\n1047\t    results = {\n1048\t        key_a: _visual_result(key_a, unit_id, \"deterministic\"),\n1049\t        key_b: _visual_result(key_b, unit_id, \"deterministic\"),\n1050\t    }\n1051\t    if mutation == \"missing\":\n1052\t        results.pop(key_b)\n1053\t    elif mutation == \"extra\":\n1054\t        extra = f\"{unit_id}/visual/det-z\"\n1055\t        results[extra] = _visual_result(extra, unit_id, \"deterministic\")\n1056\t    elif mutation == \"stale_parent\":\n1057\t        results[key_b] = {**results[key_b], \"content_hash\": \"superseded-content-hash\"}\n1058\t    elif mutation == \"cross_unit\":\n1059\t        results[key_b] = {**results[key_b], \"unit_id\": \"U999\"}\n1060\t\n1061\t    state = _visual_state(unit_id, briefs, results)\n1062\t    update = visuals.D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN(state, _Context())\n1063\t    failure = update[\"pending_failure\"]\n1064\t    assert failure[\"class\"] == \"system\"\n1065\t    assert failure[\"cause\"] in (\"join\", \"integrity\")\n1066\t    assert \"artifact_heads\" not in update\n1067\t\n1068\t\n1069\t@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n1070\t    \"mutation\",\n1071\t    [\"missing\", \"extra\", \"stale\", \"cross_unit\"],\n1072\t)\n1073\tdef test_the_source_join_refuses_a_denominator_that_is_not_exact(mutation: str) -> None:\n1074\t    \"\"\"Spec 10: the source join accepts only `actual_keys == expected_keys`.\"\"\"\n1075\t\n1076\t    unit_id = \"U001\"\n1077\t    key_a, key_b = f\"{unit_id}/1/required_explanation:000\", f\"{unit_id}/1/safety_focus:000\"\n1078\t    requests = [\n1079\t        {\"key\": key_a, \"unit_id\": unit_id, \"required\": True, \"scope\": \"required_explanation\"},\n1080\t        {\"key\": key_b, \"unit_id\": unit_id, \"required\": True, \"scope\": \"safety_focus\"},\n1081\t    ]\n1082\t    retrievals = {\n1083\t        key: {\"key\": key, \"unit_id\": unit_id, \"sha256\": f\"sha-{key}\", \"locator\": \"l\", \"content_type\": \"text/html\"}\n1084\t        for key in (key_a, key_b)\n1085\t    }\n1086\t    interpretations = {\n1087\t        key: {\"key\": key, \"unit_id\": unit_id, \"retrieval_sha256\": f\"sha-{key}\", \"scope\": \"s\"}\n1088\t        for key in (key_a, key_b)\n1089\t    }\n1090\t    if mutation == \"missing\":\n1091\t        interpretations.pop(key_b)\n1092\t    elif mutation == \"extra\":\n1093\t        rogue = f\"{unit_id}/1/undeclared:000\"\n1094\t        interpretations[rogue] = {\"key\": rogue, \"unit_id\": unit_id, \"retrieval_sha256\": \"x\"}\n1095\t    elif mutation == \"stale\":\n1096\t        interpretations[key_b] = {**interpretations[key_b], \"retrieval_sha256\": \"superseded\"}\n1097\t    elif mutation == \"cross_unit\":\n1098\t        interpretations[key_b] = {**interpretations[key_b], \"unit_id\": \"U999\"}\n1099\t\n1100\t    state = {\n1101\t        \"selected_unit_id\": unit_id,\n1102\t        \"source_requests\": requests,\n1103\t        \"source_denominators\": {\n1104\t            f\"{unit_id}/1\": {\"unit_id\": unit_id, \"source_epoch\": 1, \"request_keys\": [key_a, key_b], \"size\": 2}\n1105\t        },\n1106\t        \"source_discoveries\": {},\n1107\t        \"retrievals\": retrievals,\n1108\t        \"source_interpretations\": interpretations,\n1109\t    }\n1110\t    update = sources.D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES(state, _Context())\n1111\t\n1112\t    assert \"source_admissions\" not in update\n1113\t    if mutation == \"missing\":\n1114\t        # A missing required member is an unresolved prerequisite, not an admission.\n1115\t        assert update[\"pending_guard\"][\"value\"] == \"prerequisite_unresolved\"\n1116\t        assert R.route_source_admission({**state, **update}) == \"D30_CLASSIFY_PREREQUISITE\"\n1117\t    else:\n1118\t        assert update[\"pending_failure\"][\"class\"] == \"system\"\n1119\t        assert update[\"pending_failure\"][\"cause\"] in (\"join\", \"integrity\")\n1120\t\n1121\t\n1122\tdef test_a_duplicate_fanout_member_with_a_different_body_is_an_integrity_failure() -> None:\n1123\t    \"\"\"Spec 10: duplicate equal replay is idempotent; a different duplicate is not.\"\"\"\n1124\t\n1125\t    from runtime.langgraph_factory.reducers import UnionConflict, union_disjoint\n1126\t\n1127\t    key = \"U001/visual/det-a\"\n1128\t    first = {key: _visual_result(key, \"U001\", \"deterministic\")}\n1129\t    assert union_disjoint(first, dict(first)) == first\n1130\t    with pytest.raises(UnionConflict):\n1131\t        union_disjoint(first, {key: {**first[key], \"sha256\": \"different\"}})\n1132\t\n1133\t\n1134\t@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"unit_count\", [1, 7, 41])\n1135\tdef test_one_mode_computes_the_complete_prerequisite_closure_in_manifest_order(\n1136\t    tmp_path: Path, unit_count: int\n1137\t) -> None:\n1138\t    \"\"\"Prompt TEST 2, over a real multi-unit DAG rather than a fixed fixture.\"\"\"\n1139\t\n1140\t    edges = {index: [index - 1] for index in range(2, unit_count + 1)}\n1141\t    manifest_path, _ = _synthetic_manifest(tmp_path / str(unit_count), unit_count, edges)\n1142\t    update = inputs.D02_COMPILE_EFFECTIVE_RUN(\n1143\t        _d02_state(manifest_path, \"one\", f\"U{unit_count:03d}\"), _Context()\n1144\t    )\n1145\t    closure = update[\"effective_run\"][\"target_closure\"]\n1146\t    assert closure == [f\"U{index:03d}\" for index in range(1, unit_count + 1)]\n1147\t\n1148\t    # D05 then consumes that closure in exactly that order.\n1149\t    state = {\n1150\t        \"effective_run\": update[\"effective_run\"],\n1151\t        \"cursor\": {\"manifest_ordinal\": 0, \"accepted_ordinal\": 0},\n1152\t        \"accepted_unit_receipts\": {},\n1153\t        \"unit_status\": {},\n1154\t    }\n1155\t    selection = sources.D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT(state, _Context())\n1156\t    assert selection[\"selected_unit_id\"] == closure[0]\n1157\t    assert R.route_unit_selection({**state, **selection}) == \"D06_COMPILE_SOURCE_REQUESTS\"\n1158\t\n1159\t\n1160\tdef test_a_diamond_closure_admits_each_ancestor_exactly_once(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n1161\t    manifest_path, _ = _synthetic_manifest(tmp_path, 4, {2: [1], 3: [1], 4: [2, 3]})\n1162\t    update = inputs.D02_COMPILE_EFFECTIVE_RUN(_d02_state(manifest_path, \"one\", \"U004\"), _Context())\n1163\t    closure = update[\"effective_run\"][\"target_closure\"]\n1164\t    assert sorted(closure) == [\"U001\", \"U002\", \"U003\", \"U004\"]\n1165\t    assert len(closure) == len(set(closure))\n1166\t\n1167\t\n1168\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1169\t# No success terminal anywhere in this path (prompt TEST 10)\n1170\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1171\t\n1172\t\n1173\tdef test_no_node_in_this_path_can_emit_a_product_success_terminal() -> None:\n1174\t    \"\"\"A capability, intermediate artifact, review, or clean check emits nothing.\n1175\t\n1176\t    The two product terminals (`UNIT_ACCEPTED`, `COMPLETE`) are reachable only\n1177\t    from D24/D32, neither of which this path wires; every node here that can\n1178\t    reach D98 does so with a failure, interrupt, or pause candidate.\n1179\t    \"\"\"\n1180\t\n1181\t    product_terminals = {\"UNIT_ACCEPTED\", \"COMPLETE\"}\n1182\t    for source, _guard in U.UNIT_BRANCHES:\n1183\t        spec = NODE_CATALOGUE.get(source)\n1184\t        if spec is None:\n1185\t            continue\n1186\t        module_path = REPO_ROOT / \"runtime\" / \"langgraph_factory\" / \"nodes\" / f\"{spec.module}.py\"\n1187\t        body = module_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n1188\t        for terminal in product_terminals:\n1189\t            # Word-bounded: `INCOMPLETE` is a join verdict, not a terminal kind.\n1190\t            assert not re.search(rf\"\\b{terminal}\\b\", body), f\"{source} names {terminal}\"\n1191\t\n1192\t    # Nothing this path wires reaches the acceptance node that mints a receipt.\n1193\t    reachable = {target for _s, _v, target, _o in U.DEFERRED_EDGES}\n1194\t    assert \"D22_ACCEPT_UNIT\" not in reachable\n1195\t    assert not set(U.unit_path_nodes()) & {\"D22_ACCEPT_UNIT\", \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\"}\n1196\t\n1197\t\n1198\tdef test_the_model_path_uses_only_a_test_transport_and_no_product_output_root() -> None:\n1199\t    \"\"\"A fake transport is injectable only through the explicitly named builder.\"\"\"\n1200\t\n1201\t    sandbox = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp())\n1202\t    context = mn.build_test_model_node_context(sandbox_root=sandbox, responses={})\n1203\t    assert isinstance(context.transport, mn.tp.FakeCliTransport)\n1204\t    with pytest.raises(mn.ModelNodeError):\n1205\t        mn.build_model_node_context(\n1206\t            type(\"_C\", (), {\"transport_registry\": context.transport})()  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n1207\t        )\n1208\t\n1209\t\n1210\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1211\t# Real execution of the real compiled graph (prompt TEST 1, and the reachable\n1212\t# part of TEST 9). Every assertion below runs one real `.stream()`.\n1213\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1214\t\n1215\t\n1216\t# The bootstrap prefix, which is a contiguous run of single-successor nodes and\n1217\t# so can be asserted as a literal prefix of the trace.\n1218\tBOOTSTRAP_SPINE = (\n1219\t    \"D00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE\",\n1220\t    \"D01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS\",\n1221\t    \"D02_COMPILE_EFFECTIVE_RUN\",\n1222\t    \"D03_PROVE_CAPABILITIES\",\n1223\t    \"D04_INITIALIZE_OR_RESUME\",\n1224\t    \"D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT\",\n1225\t    \"D06_COMPILE_SOURCE_REQUESTS\",\n1226\t)\n1227\t\n1228\t# Every node, map and barrier boundary a real episode currently reaches, in the\n1229\t# order it is first entered. Past D06 the path is no longer a simple spine: D90\n1230\t# reserves before each dispatch, M01 runs as a two-member `Send` map twice, and\n1231\t# D07/D08 are join barriers. Prompt TEST 9 is parametrized over this whole set,\n1232\t# so the crash matrix covers map and barrier boundaries and not just plain nodes.\n1233\tREACHABLE_BOUNDARIES = BOOTSTRAP_SPINE + (\n1234\t    \"D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT\",\n1235\t    \"M01_RESEARCH_UNIT_SOURCES\",\n1236\t    \"D06B_RETRIEVE_SOURCE_CANDIDATES\",\n1237\t    \"D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES\",\n1238\t    \"M02_CREATE_UNIT_DOMAIN_DATA\",\n1239\t    \"D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN\",\n1240\t    \"M03_WRITE_UNIT_CONTENT\",\n1241\t    \"D09_VALIDATE_CONTENT\",\n1242\t    \"D10_COMPILE_VISUAL_BRIEFS\",\n1243\t    \"D11_CREATE_DETERMINISTIC_VISUALS\",\n1244\t    \"D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN\",\n1245\t    \"M04_CREATE_UNIT_VISUALS\",\n1246\t    \"D13_RENDER_UNIT\",\n1247\t    \"D14_INVENTORY_AND_INSPECT_UNIT_PAGES\",\n1248\t    \"D15_FREEZE_UNIT_REVIEW_PACKET\",\n1249\t)\n1250\t\n1251\t# M05 runs — its receipt, its candidate record and its page findings are all in\n1252\t# the committed state — but its update never reaches a stream consumer, because\n1253\t# the branch that would emit it resolves to `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE`, this\n1254\t# node's declared handoff to N31, and aborts the superstep first. It is therefore\n1255\t# not an observable interrupt boundary and is excluded from the matrix above\n1256\t# rather than asserted vacuously. The same was true of D09 until B-10 was fixed\n1257\t# and the frontier moved past it.\n1258\tUNOBSERVABLE_BOUNDARY = \"M05_REVIEW_ACTUAL_UNIT\"\n1259\t\n1260\t\n1261\tdef test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_langgraph(\n1262\t    tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch\n1263\t) -> None:\n1264\t    \"\"\"Prompt TEST 1: the fresh path really runs, and D01 runs exactly once.\"\"\"\n1265\t\n1266\t    fixture = _build_episode_fixture(tmp_path)\n1267\t    result = _run_episode(monkeypatch, fixture)\n1268\t\n1269\t    assert result[\"trace\"][: len(BOOTSTRAP_SPINE)] == list(BOOTSTRAP_SPINE)\n1270\t    assert result[\"trace\"].count(\"D01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS\") == 1\n1271\t    assert \"D00R_REVALIDATE_RESUME_IDENTITY\" not in result[\"trace\"]\n1272\t    assert \"D92_REENTER_VALIDATED_FRONTIER\" not in result[\"trace\"]\n1273\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NeCmjuxKDcAbksKJ6Yq96c","session_id":"913d8145-a69b-41ae-866d-8d539cb6c5e2","uuid":"929e9c59-249e-47c1-879f-bec6423afe4c","timestamp":"2026-08-12T15:12:39.852Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write test_plan26_adversarial.py"}
