{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ey6Qir1nzXrTZEaR5uzHFQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"N40 CLI cutover proof: `runtime.run_curriculum` as the sole production entry.\n2\t\n3\tCovers the node's own TEST checklist:\n4\t\n5\t1. static + runtime call-graph proof of one production graph builder/path\n6\t2. CLI help exposes no legacy simulation/session-bridge/custom-controller path\n7\t3. mode mutual exclusion, arguments, canonical paths, collision/resume rules,\n8\t   stdout JSON, stderr diagnostics, and exit codes\n9\t4. preflight is read-only and cannot emit product success\n10\t5. CLI code contains no product nodes, guards, joins, acceptance, or frontier\n11\t   selection\n12\t6. missing authorization/capability fails before transmission and never\n13\t   simulates\n14\t7. existing Plan 25 roots are readable history but refused for Plan 26 resume\n15\t8. production import audit rejects LangChain wrappers/provider SDKs/direct\n16\t   model HTTP\n17\t\n18\tThe heavy graph/transport machinery (real LangGraph compilation, real model\n19\ttransport, real checkpoint durability) is proven elsewhere (N20/N21/N30/N32's\n20\town suites); this module proves the CLI *wires* those pieces correctly, using\n21\tthe real persistence layer wherever it is cheap and safe to do so (no model\n22\tsubprocess, no network) and narrow mocks only where a real call would need a\n23\tlive Codex/Gemini installation this environment does not have.\n24\t\"\"\"\n25\t\n26\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n27\t\n28\timport ast\n29\timport io\n30\timport json\n31\timport re\n32\timport unittest\n33\tfrom contextlib import redirect_stderr, redirect_stdout\n34\tfrom pathlib import Path\n35\tfrom types import SimpleNamespace\n36\tfrom unittest import mock\n37\t\n38\tfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import persistence as P\n39\tfrom runtime.langgraph_factory import transport as tp\n40\t\n41\timport runtime.run_curriculum as R\n42\t\n43\tREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n44\tCLI_SOURCE_PATH = REPO_ROOT / \"runtime\" / \"run_curriculum.py\"\n45\tCLI_SOURCE = CLI_SOURCE_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n46\tCLI_AST = ast.parse(CLI_SOURCE, filename=str(CLI_SOURCE_PATH))\n47\t\n48\t\n49\tdef _run_main(argv: list[str]) -> tuple[int, dict, str]:\n50\t    out, err = io.StringIO(), io.StringIO()\n51\t    with redirect_stdout(out), redirect_stderr(err):\n52\t        code = R.main(argv)\n53\t    text = out.getvalue()\n54\t    assert text.count(\"\\n\") == 1, f\"expected exactly one JSON line on stdout, got: {text!r}\"\n55\t    return code, json.loads(text), err.getvalue()\n56\t\n57\t\n58\tdef _authorization_file(tmp_path: Path, **overrides) -> Path:\n59\t    payload = {\n60\t        \"approved_at_utc\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00+00:00\","}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NeCmjuxKDcAbksKJ6Yq96c","session_id":"913d8145-a69b-41ae-866d-8d539cb6c5e2","uuid":"69a0601a-d167-4c5b-9dcb-a1f70452ffed","timestamp":"2026-08-12T15:13:05.008Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write test_plan26_adversarial.py"}
